        "1593": {"comment":"Moved: stored, the column remembered"},
        "1596": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1599": {"synopsis":"Places column B of row C in the row's text: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT, and TEXT_END_LEFT when that\nfails.\nExit: carry when the row has text. Keeps DE."},
        "1600": {"comment":"At or right of column B?"},
        "1603": {"comment":"Otherwise left of it"},
        "1608": {"synopsis":"As COL_PLACE_R, the other way round: TEXT_END_LEFT first, then TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT.\nExit: carry when the row has text. Keeps DE."},
        "1609": {"comment":"Left of column B?"},
        "1612": {"comment":"Otherwise at or right of it"},
        "1617": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C up one:\n1. Leaving the first row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_FIRST_ROW); a report stops\n   the move.\n2. A row C with no text is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW).\n3. With C below the top limit ($D748), C - 1. Otherwise the rows scroll down\n   (ROWS_SCROLL_DOWN) and C stays; with nothing above, C - 1 unless C is 0.\nExit: carry when moved.","comment":"Leaving the line's first row: entered"},
        "1620": {"comment":"A report: no move"},
        "1622": {"comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "1623": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "1626": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "1628": {"comment":"No text: the row removed"},
        "1634": {"comment":"The cursor back"},
        "1635": {"comment":"HL = the top limit"},
        "1638": {"comment":"A = it"},
