        "1729": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place right within the text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT). Past\nthe row's end:\n1. While rows may be added ($D5B7 bit 7 clear) and the row does not continue (flags bit 1),\n   it is marked as continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared) and gone through ($11A9); the cursor\n   goes down (ROW_DOWN) and a blank row is inserted there (INSERT_ROW, flags bit 3 set) with\n   its first ($D7D8) columns cleared ($100C).\n2. Otherwise down a row (ROW_DOWN) to the start of its text.\nExit: carry when it moved, A = the column.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "1730": {"comment":"One column right"},
