        "2006": {"comment":"No: on, with carry"},
        "2008": {"synopsis":"Enters the edited line the cursor is on (also from NextZXOS ROM 0's RUN_COMMAND at $097C,\nwith C = 0):\n1. Up from row C to the line's first row (flags bit 0): the reader's state 2 (window rows)\n   from there; above row 0, state 1 (the rows above the window) from row 0.\n2. The reader's state (bit 7 set), column 0 and row stored at $D5AF and kept at $D5B2; $D5B5\n   = 0.\n3. In bank 0, $5B6C = $0B91 and ERR_SP pointing at $5B3A; then $14EE in bank 7.\n4. With the word at $D7F3 above $0500 the line is not entered: ENTER_DIFF.\n5. Otherwise it is entered (ROM 1's LINE_ENTER, $09FE, IX kept, interrupts on). No report:\n   $D5B7 bit 3 cleared, the key mode reset (ROM 0's KEY_MODE_RESET), the rows rebuilt, a\n   high beep (ROM 0's BEEP_HIGH), the cursor's place in C, B, A, carry.\n6. A report (ERR_NR not $FF): the reader set back (ENTER_FAILED), $14EA, and the cursor\n   moved by the difference between ($D5B5) and BC (ENTER_DIFF).\nExit: carry when entered.","comment":"State 2: the window's rows"},
        "2010": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "2013": {"comment":"HL = the width"},
        "2016": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "2017": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "2021": {"comment":"The row above"},
        "2022": {"comment":"Not above row 0 yet"},
        "2025": {"comment":"Row 0"},
        "2027": {"comment":"State 1: the rows above the window"},
        "2029": {"synopsis":"The reader's state, column 0 and row, twice.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "2032": {"comment":"DE = its copy"},
        "2035": {"comment":"Bit 7: count the places"},
        "2037": {"comment":"The state stored twice"},
        "2039": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "2046": {"comment":"Row C"},
        "2049": {"comment":"No places counted yet"},
        "2055": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the normal stack"},
