        "2662": {"synopsis":"Deletes the character at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving left\nacross its rows:\n1. Down to the line's last row (flags bit 1 clear); past the window's last row, the rows\n   below give back their first character (BELOW_PULL).\n2. From the last row up to the cursor's row, each row loses its first character (column B on\n   the cursor's row: ROW_PULL_CHAR) and takes the one from the row below at its end; a later\n   row left empty is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW).\n3. A line left empty on its first row clears $D5B7 bit 3.\nExit: A = 0. Keeps BC."},
        "2663": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
