        "3342": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "3343": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3345": {"synopsis":"Carries character A, pushed off the end of the window's last row (HL = that row's flags\nbyte), into the rows below the window, row 1 on: each row takes it at its text's start\n(ROW_PUSH_CHAR) and passes on what falls off its end; when nothing more falls off, the count\n= C and row C ends the line (bit 3). A row that ended the line gets a new row after it\n(cleared from column B, flags 8, its first ($D7D8) columns cleared); a full buffer ($0EEE)\nsets $D5B7 bit 0 (the rows are full).","comment":"Row 1"},
        "3348": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3350": {"comment":"DE = row 1 below the window"},
        "3353": {"comment":"HL = the last row's flags byte"},
        "3354": {"comment":"Was it the line's last row?"},
        "3356": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "3358": {"comment":"Yes: a new row needed"},
        "3360": {"synopsis":"B moved over the row's empty cells (TEXT_FROM_COL).","comment":"From column 0"},
        "3362": {"comment":"B = the start of the row's text"},
        "3365": {"synopsis":"A inserted at column B of row DE (ROW_PUSH_CHAR).","comment":"The character back"},
        "3366": {"comment":"In at column B"},
        "3370": {"comment":"The character pushed off kept"},
        "3371": {"comment":"Flags: B added"},
        "3374": {"comment":"Gone through"},
        "3377": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte, DE = the row"},
        "3378": {"comment":"The character back"},
        "3379": {"comment":"Nothing pushed off: done"},
        "3381": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3383": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3384": {"comment":"Room for it?"},
        "3387": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "3390": {"comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "3393": {"comment":"The rows full"},
        "3396": {"synopsis":"The row marked as continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared); DE = row C; a row that was not\ncontinued is made new.","comment":"Was the row continued?"},
        "3398": {"comment":"Continued now"},
        "3400": {"comment":"Not the line's last row"},
        "3402": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3405": {"comment":"Continued: into that row"},
        "3409": {"comment":"The row cleared from column B"},
        "3412": {"comment":"Flags 8: the line's last row"},
        "3416": {"comment":"Its first ($D7D8) columns cleared"},
        "3419": {"comment":"In at column B"},
        "3421": {"synopsis":"Nothing more pushed off: the count = C, bit 3 on row C's flags.","comment":"A = the row"},
        "3422": {"comment":"The count of rows below"},
        "3425": {"comment":"The line's last row"},
        "3428": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the rows below the window: $C73B + ($D73F) x C (ROW_ADDRESS_HL).\nExit: HL = ($D73F). Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the rows below the window"},
        "3431": {"comment":"DE = row C of them"},
        "3434": {"synopsis":"Pulls the rows below the window one character back, from the last row ($C738) up to row 1:\nin each row the character at its text's start is taken out (ROW_PULL_CHAR) with the one\ncarried put in at its end. A row left empty is dropped: its flags go to the row before (row\nC - 1, or for row 1 the window's last row), bit 1 cleared there, and the count drops.\nExit: A = the character taken from row 1; carry. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3436": {"comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "3439": {"comment":"The rows not full any more"},
        "3441": {"comment":"A = the count of rows below"},
        "3444": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "3445": {"comment":"None?"},
        "3446": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "3448": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "3450": {"synopsis":"Row C: DE = its address; its first used column found (TEXT_FROM_COL).","comment":"DE = row C below the window"},
        "3453": {"comment":"The character carried kept"},
        "3454": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3456": {"comment":"Text in the row from column 0 ($09A2)?"},
        "3459": {"comment":"No: the row dropped"},
        "3461": {"comment":"The character from the row below in at the end ($02C9)"},
        "3462": {"comment":"Its first character out, A in at the end"},
        "3465": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out at column B; still text?"},
        "3467": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3469": {"comment":"Any text left?"},
        "3473": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "3475": {"synopsis":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before.","comment":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before"},
        "3476": {"comment":"A = the dropped row's flags"},
        "3479": {"comment":"Row 1 of the buffer?"},
        "3480": {"comment":"Row 1?"},
        "3484": {"comment":"Then the row before is the window's last ($D73C)"},
        "3487": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "3488": {"comment":"DE = the window's last row"},
        "3491": {"comment":"On"},
        "3493": {"synopsis":"The row before: row C - 1 of the buffer.","comment":"Else row C - 1 of the buffer"},
        "3494": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "3497": {"synopsis":"The row before: bit 1 cleared, the dropped row's flags added; the count one less."},
        "3499": {"comment":"HL = the row before's flags byte"},
        "3502": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "3503": {"comment":"Not continued; the dropped row's flags added"},
        "3505": {"comment":"The dropped row's flags added"},
        "3507": {"comment":"One row fewer below the window"},
        "3510": {"comment":"One less"},
        "3511": {"synopsis":"The row above, until row 1 is done.","comment":"A = the character to carry"},
        "3512": {"comment":"The row above, until row 1 is done"},
        "3513": {"comment":"Until row 1 is done"},
        "3515": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "3516": {"synopsis":"DE and BC back; return (with carry when the rows moved, from $0DBB; as entered from $0D78)."},
        "3519": {"synopsis":"ABOVE_INIT's bytes for COPY_COUNTED ($045A): a count (3), then $00 for $CE73 (the count of\nrows kept above the window) and $CE76 for $CE74-$CE75 (the pointer past the top row)."},
        "3523": {"synopsis":"Empties the stack of rows kept above the window: $CE73 (the count) = 0 and $CE74 (the\npointer past the top row) = $CE76, the stack's first row, copied from ABOVE_INIT_DATA by\nCOPY_COUNTED ($045A). From $0136, $01F9 and $0369.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The bytes, a count first"},
        "3526": {"comment":"To $CE73-$CE75"},
        "3532": {"synopsis":"Takes the row nearest the window off the stack of rows above it ($CE73 the count, $CE74 the\npointer past the top row, rows ($D73F) bytes long from $CE76):\n1. With rows on the stack: the pointer moves back one row and the count goes down by one.\n2. With none: the program line before line ($D74E) is found (EXPAND_INIT, PREV_LINE_NUM);\n   when there is one, $D74E = its number, it is written into rows from $CE76 (LINE_TO_ROWS)\n   and its last row is the one taken, the others staying on the stack.\nExit: carry and HL = the row's address; no carry when there is no row. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3534": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "3537": {"comment":"Kept for ABOVE_STORE"},
        "3538": {"comment":"Rows on the stack?"},
        "3542": {"comment":"None: the expansion reset"},
        "3546": {"comment":"The line before the top line"},
        "3549": {"comment":"PREV_LINE_NUM: HL = its number or 0"},
        "3552": {"comment":"Found: it is the top line now"},
        "3557": {"synopsis":"BC = the line found (or 0)."},
        "3559": {"comment":"HL = $CE76, the stack's first row"},
        "3560": {"comment":"HL = $CE76"},
        "3563": {"comment":"No line: no carry"},
        "3565": {"comment":"HL = $CE73 again"},
        "3568": {"comment":"The line into rows from $CE76; A = the rows"},
        "3571": {"comment":"The last row taken off: count = rows - 1, DE = it"},
        "3572": {"comment":"DE = the line's last row"},
        "3575": {"synopsis":"A row off the stack: the pointer back by one row (($D73F) bytes).","comment":"The pointer past the top row"},
        "3578": {"comment":"BC = the row length"},
        "3584": {"comment":"Carry; the count one less"},
        "3586": {"synopsis":"With carry: the count = A and the pointer = DE.\nExit: HL = DE; BC, DE back."},
        "3587": {"comment":"HL = $CE73, the count"},
        "3588": {"comment":"No carry: nothing stored"},
        "3590": {"comment":"The count stored"},
        "3591": {"synopsis":"The pointer = DE."},
        "3592": {"comment":"The pointer stored"},
        "3595": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "3596": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "3599": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE on the stack of rows above the window ($CE73):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, its line number (the two bytes after the\n   flags, high byte first) goes to $D74E.\n2. A line's last row (flags bit 3) empties the stack instead: $D74E becomes the number of\n   the line after it (EXPAND_INIT, NEXT_LINE_NUM; 0 when there is none), the count 0 and the\n   pointer $CE76.\n3. Otherwise the row is copied on top when one more fits (ROWS_FIT) and the count goes up; a\n   full stack keeps it out.\nExit: carry when the stack changed. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3601": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "3604": {"comment":"The flags byte"},
        "3606": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "3609": {"comment":"Not both: no line number taken"},
        "3613": {"comment":"Its line number, high byte first"},
        "3617": {"comment":"$D74E = that line"},
        "3621": {"comment":"HL = the flags, DE = the row again"},
        "3623": {"synopsis":"A line's last row (bit 3) empties the stack."},
        "3625": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "3629": {"comment":"Not a last row: kept on the stack"},
        "3632": {"comment":"The expansion reset"},
        "3635": {"comment":"The line after the top line (0 when none)"},
        "3641": {"comment":"$D74E = that line, or 0"},
        "3645": {"comment":"HL = $CE76; count 0, carry"},
        "3648": {"comment":"Count 0, carry: stored"},
        "3652": {"synopsis":"The row copied on top, when there is room.","comment":"C = the count"},
        "3653": {"comment":"One more row fits?"},
        "3656": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "3657": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "3659": {"comment":"The count + 1"},
        "3660": {"comment":"The row copied to the pointer"},
        "3663": {"comment":"BC = the row length"},
        "3667": {"comment":"From the row at DE"},
        "3670": {"comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "3671": {"comment":"Carry: count and pointer stored"},
        "3674": {"synopsis":"Full: the row is not kept."},
        "3675": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "3678": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the stack above the window: $CE76 + ($D73F) x C (ROW_ADDRESS_HL at $0C54).\nKeeps AF, BC. From $08FE and $0B41."},
        "3681": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL"},
        "3684": {"synopsis":"Writes the program line being expanded (EXPAND_NEXT; set up by NEXT_LINE_START or\nPREV_LINE_START) into editor rows from HL + 3, BC its line number:\n1. The first row's flags = $21 (bits 0 and 5) and the number after them, high byte first.\n2. Each character goes in at column B (ROW_PUT_CHAR). A keyword's characters (B = 1 from\n   EXPAND_NEXT) are stored as codes: a letter less $3B, '#' or '$' less $1F, and the R of\n   REM ($D760 = $EA) as 3.\n3. A full row ends with its flags XOR $12 (ROW_NEW) and the next is indented (ROW_INDENT);\n   no room ends the line.\n4. ENTER, or the end of the text, ends the row (ROW_END_LINE; ROW_END_EMPTY for a line with\n   no text).\nWith the state byte ($D5B8) not 0 no text is read.\nExit: carry, HL = the first row, A = the rows.\nChanges: BC, DE.","comment":"DE = HL + 3, the first row"},
        "3689": {"comment":"Kept: the first row"},
        "3690": {"comment":"HL = its flags byte"},
        "3694": {"comment":"The line's first row, a statement starting"},
        "3696": {"comment":"The line number after the flags"},
        "3700": {"comment":"Column 0, one row"},
        "3703": {"synopsis":"The next character, unless the state byte ($D5B8) is not 0."},
        "3705": {"comment":"The state byte"},
        "3709": {"comment":"EXPAND_NEXT: carry, A = a character"},
        "3712": {"comment":"Z: a keyword's character"},
        "3713": {"comment":"DE, BC back; the flags kept"},
        "3715": {"comment":"Carry: a character came"},
        "3717": {"comment":"Nothing on a single row?"},
        "3720": {"comment":"Text written: ROW_END_LINE"},
        "3722": {"comment":"An empty line"},
        "3725": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3727": {"synopsis":"The line's end: the row ended (ROW_END_LINE)."},
        "3730": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3732": {"synopsis":"A character: a keyword's (Z) is stored as a code."},
        "3734": {"comment":"An R"},
        "3736": {"comment":"Another letter"},
        "3738": {"comment":"After REM ($EA)?"},
        "3741": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "3743": {"comment":"Otherwise 'R' less $3B"},
        "3745": {"comment":"Not after REM"},
        "3747": {"comment":"REM's R: 3"},
        "3749": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3751": {"synopsis":"A keyword's other characters: a letter less $3B, '#' or '$' less $1F."},
        "3753": {"comment":"A letter"},
        "3755": {"comment":"'#' or '$': less $1F"},
        "3757": {"synopsis":"Text: ENTER ends the line."},
