        "3767": {"comment":"Column B not past it: stored"},
        "3769": {"comment":"Full: continued, a new row"},
        "3771": {"comment":"ROW_NEW with bits 1 and 4 flipped"},
        "3774": {"comment":"Room: the new row indented"},
        "3776": {"comment":"No room: the line ends"},
        "3779": {"synopsis":"The new row indented."},
        "3782": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B; the next."},
        "3786": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "3788": {"synopsis":"HL = the first row, A = the rows; carry."},
        "3789": {"comment":"A = the rows"},
        "3793": {"synopsis":"Ends row DE (ROW_CLEAR_REST) with its flags XOR A and starts the next: the row's syntax\nstate at its end (ROW_END_STATE) becomes the next row's flags, C + 1, DE + ($D73F).\nExit: carry, HL = the new row's flags byte; no carry when no more rows fit (ROWS_FIT).\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "3794": {"comment":"The rest of the row cleared"},
        "3798": {"comment":"Its flags XOR A"},
        "3799": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3800": {"comment":"HL = the row, for ROW_END_STATE"},
        "3801": {"comment":"B = the state at the row's end"},
        "3804": {"comment":"DE = the row again"},
        "3805": {"comment":"Room for another row?"},
        "3808": {"comment":"No room: no carry"},
        "3809": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3810": {"comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "3815": {"comment":"Its flags = the state carried on"},
        "3820": {"comment":"Carry: a new row"},
        "3822": {"synopsis":"Do C + 1 rows of ($D73F) bytes fit in $0738 bytes, the size of each row buffer? Exit: carry\nwhen they do. Keeps BC, DE, HL."},
        "3824": {"comment":"E = the row length"},
        "3828": {"comment":"D = C + 1"},
        "3830": {"comment":"DE = (C + 1) x row length"},
        "3832": {"comment":"The buffer's size"},
        "3836": {"comment":"Do they fit?"},
        "3838": {"comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "3840": {"comment":"Carry: they fit"},
        "3842": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of the program line after line HL (HL = 0: the first line) for\nEXPAND_NEXT: EXPAND_INIT, then with bank 0 the line numbered HL found (LINE_FIND_EXACT) and\nthe one after it taken; on to LINE_START_SET. From NEXT_LINE_NUM.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry when there is no such line\n(or no line after it). Bank 7 on exit."},
        "3843": {"comment":"The expansion reset; RAM routines copied"},
        "3846": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "3847": {"comment":"Bank 0: the program"},
        "3848": {"comment":"Line HL there?"},
        "3851": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "3855": {"comment":"HL = 0: the first line itself"},
        "3859": {"comment":"Else the line after it"},
        "3862": {"comment":"Is there one?"},
        "3865": {"comment":"None after it: no carry"},
        "3867": {"synopsis":"For the line at HL: DE = its number (high byte first), then LINE_START_NUM."},
        "3868": {"comment":"DE = the line number"},
        "3870": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "3871": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of a line, DE its number and HL its address + 1: the number as four\ncharacters at $D767 (LINE_NUM_DIGIT; leading zeros as 0 bytes), then $A0 (a space, the\nlast); $D765 = $D767, the text to give first; $D763 = HL + 3, the line's text. From $1A0A\nand $1A27 too.\nExit: carry, HL = the number, DE = the line's text. Keeps IX."},
        "3873": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "3875": {"comment":"The number's text at $D767"},
        "3879": {"comment":"Given first by EXPAND_NEXT"},
        "3883": {"comment":"HL = the number; no digit seen yet"},
        "3886": {"comment":"Thousands"},
        "3889": {"comment":"The digit for 1000s"},
        "3892": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "3898": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "3904": {"comment":"Units"},
        "3910": {"comment":"A space with bit 7: the text's end"},
        "3914": {"comment":"IX, HL, DE back"},
        "3918": {"comment":"HL = the line's text"},
        "3921": {"comment":"The place in the program"},
        "3924": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "3925": {"comment":"Carry: set up"},
        "3927": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 again; the flags as they are."},
        "3928": {"comment":"Flags as they were"},
        "3929": {"synopsis":"One decimal digit of HL into (IX), DE being minus its place's value (-1000, -100, -10, -1):\na 0 before any other digit is stored as 0 (B = 0), later ones as '0' (B = 1).\nExit: HL keeps the rest, IX + 1."},
        "3930": {"synopsis":"DE added while it fits; A counts."},
        "3931": {"comment":"A counts the subtractions"},
        "3932": {"comment":"While HL stays positive"},
        "3934": {"comment":"One too many: back"},
        "3936": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "3937": {"comment":"The digit as a character"},
        "3939": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3942": {"comment":"A '0'"},
