        "4038": {"comment":"Still in the program?"},
        "4041": {"comment":"The end: no carry, DE = the last line"},
        "4042": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "4047": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "4048": {"synopsis":"ROW_SETUP's bytes for COPY_COUNTED ($045A): a count (2), then 1 for $D7D7 and 5 for $D7D8."},
        "4051": {"synopsis":"$D7D7 = 1 and $D7D8 = 5 (the cells a line's later rows are indented by, ROW_INDENT), copied\nfrom ROW_SETUP_DATA by COPY_COUNTED ($045A). From $0348.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "4060": {"synopsis":"Puts A in column B of row DE; B + 1.\nChanges: HL."},
        "4063": {"comment":"HL = column B's cell"},
        "4065": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "4067": {"synopsis":"Ends a line's text in row DE: the rest of the row cleared (ROW_CLEAR_REST), its flags' bits\n3 and 4 set, $D7D7 bit 0 set.\nExit: carry, NZ."},
        "4070": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4: the line's last row"},
        "4074": {"comment":"$D7D7 bit 0: a line's end written"},
        "4081": {"synopsis":"As ROW_END_LINE for a line with no text: only bit 3 of the flags set.\nExit: carry, Z."},
        "4084": {"comment":"Bit 3: the line's last row"},
        "4093": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's cells from column B to the last ($D73D, the column count) to 0.\nExit: B = the column count, HL = the row's flags byte, Z.","comment":"HL = column B's cell"},
        "4097": {"comment":"A = the column count"},
        "4100": {"synopsis":"Up to the last column."},
        "4101": {"comment":"Done: Z"},
        "4102": {"comment":"Cleared; the next"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's first ($D7D8) cells.\nExit: B = ($D7D8), the column after them.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "4111": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4113": {"synopsis":"One cell."},
        "4120": {"comment":"Until the indent is done"},
        "4124": {"synopsis":"Unless $D741 bit 2 is set (no screen output): SCROLL_UP with E = C, which moves window lines\nB + 1 to C one line up and prints the row at HL on line C. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4128": {"comment":"Screen output off?"},
        "4133": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4137": {"comment":"SCROLL_UP with E = C"},
        "4140": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back."},
        "4144": {"synopsis":"Unless $D741 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_DOWN with E = C, which moves window lines B to C - 1 one\nline down and prints the row at HL on line B. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4148": {"comment":"Screen output off?"},
        "4153": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4157": {"comment":"SCROLL_DOWN with E = C"},
        "4160": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back."},
        "4164": {"synopsis":"Marks the cell at column B, line C: WIN_CURSOR_ON with B and C swapped for it. Keeps all\nregisters."},
        "4168": {"comment":"B = line, C = column"},
        "4174": {"comment":"All back"},
        "4179": {"synopsis":"Takes the mark CELL_CURSOR_ON made off the cell at column B, line C (WIN_CURSOR_OFF). Keeps\nall registers."},
        "4183": {"comment":"B = line, C = column"},
        "4189": {"comment":"All back"},
        "4194": {"synopsis":"The editor's window for the main screen, copied to $D7D9 (IX) by WINDOW_SET: a count (8),\nthen 0, 0 (its top line), 20 (its last row, from the top) and five 0s."},
        "4203": {"synopsis":"The window for the lower screen: a count (8), then 0, 22 (its top line), 1 (its last row)\nand five 0s."},
        "4212": {"synopsis":"IX = $D7D9, the window there from WINDOW_MAIN_DATA (main screen, lines 0-20). From $0437."},
        "4216": {"comment":"Main screen's window"},
        "4221": {"synopsis":"The window at $D7D9 from WINDOW_LOW_DATA (lines 22-23). From $0425."},
        "4224": {"synopsis":"The 8 bytes at HL to $D7D9 (COPY_COUNTED, $045A)."},
        "4227": {"comment":"COPY_COUNTED"},
        "4230": {"synopsis":"IX + 6 = the cursor's kind from ROM 0's CURSOR_KIND (from MODE, or caps lock), the index\ninto the cursor colours at $D6E8 (CURSOR_KIND_PUT). Keeps AF. From $0482, $051C and $054C."},
        "4231": {"comment":"ROM 0's CURSOR_KIND: A = the kind"},
        "4234": {"comment":"IX + 6 = it"},
        "4239": {"synopsis":"IX + 6 = A; carry."},
        "4244": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at line B of the window (IX + 1 added), column C: the attribute there kept\nin IX + 7 and replaced by the colour at $D6E8 + the cursor's kind (IX + 6). In a Timex mode\n($5C7F bit 3) the cursor is drawn as a character instead (CURSOR_XOR_CHAR).\nExit: carry.","comment":"B = the screen line"},
        "4249": {"comment":"A Timex mode?"},
        "4255": {"comment":"HL = its attribute"},
        "4258": {"comment":"Kept in IX + 7"},
        "4262": {"comment":"The colour for the cursor's kind"},
        "4265": {"comment":"The cursor colours from $D6E8"},
        "4271": {"comment":"The cursor's colour in"},
        "4274": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off line B of the window, column C: the attribute kept in IX + 7 put back;\nin a Timex mode the character is drawn again (CURSOR_XOR_CHAR), which takes it off.","comment":"B = the screen line"},
        "4277": {"comment":"A Timex mode?"},
        "4281": {"comment":"Draw the character again"},
        "4283": {"comment":"HL = the attribute address"},
        "4286": {"comment":"The attribute kept"},
        "4289": {"comment":"Put back"},
        "4291": {"synopsis":"Draws the cursor at line B, column C with OVER 1, so that drawing it twice takes it off: UDG\n= ROM 0's own pictures (UDG_ROM_GLYPHS), AT B, C (ROM 0's $07BA), OVER 1, the character $92\n+ the kind (IX + 6; ROM 0's CURSOR_CODE), OVER 0, and UDG back (UDG_SWAP).","comment":"ROM 0's UDG_ROM_GLYPHS: HL = the old UDG"},
        "4294": {"comment":"The old UDG kept"},
        "4295": {"comment":"ROM 0's $07BA: AT B, C"},
        "4298": {"comment":"OVER 1"},
        "4304": {"comment":"The cursor's picture, $92 + its kind"},
        "4307": {"comment":"ROM 0's CURSOR_CODE: A + $92"},
        "4310": {"comment":"The picture printed"},
        "4311": {"comment":"OVER 0"},
        "4316": {"comment":"ROM 0's UDG_SWAP: UDG back"},
        "4321": {"synopsis":"In a Timex mode ($5C7F bit 3): B + the window's top line (WIN_LINE_ADD); otherwise nothing.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4325": {"comment":"Not a Timex mode: B as it is"},
        "4326": {"synopsis":"B = B + IX + 1: line B of the window as a screen line.\nChanges: A."},
        "4329": {"comment":"B + the window's top line"},
        "4332": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E up by one (pixels and attributes, each line from the one\nbelow), then prints the row at HL on line E (SCROLL_PRINT)."},
        "4333": {"comment":"H = 0: up"},
        "4335": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "4337": {"comment":"On to the scroll"},
        "4339": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E down by one (B the upper; each line from the one above,\nstarting at E), then prints the row at HL on line B."},
        "4340": {"comment":"B and E swapped: start at E"},
        "4343": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "4344": {"comment":"H = $FF: down"},
        "4346": {"synopsis":"C = the lines to move; none when B = E."},
        "4347": {"comment":"Only one line?"},
        "4349": {"comment":"Just the row printed"},
        "4351": {"comment":"E kept: the line freed"},
        "4352": {"comment":"B = the line as ROM 3 counts lines"},
        "4355": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR), and the source's, one below (up)\nor one above (down)."},
        "4356": {"comment":"C = the direction"},
        "4357": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = line B"},
        "4360": {"comment":"DE = the line moved into"},
        "4361": {"comment":"Up or down?"},
        "4365": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "4368": {"synopsis":"Up: the line below."},
        "4369": {"synopsis":"Its 8 pixel rows copied, 32 bytes each, then its 32 attributes."},
        "4370": {"comment":"HL = the source line"},
        "4373": {"comment":"DE = the line moved into"},
        "4374": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "4375": {"comment":"32 bytes a pixel row"},
        "4377": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4379": {"comment":"A Timex mode: two display files"},
        "4385": {"comment":"Bank $0B at $6000 (ROM 0's MMU3_SWAP)"},
        "4388": {"comment":"A' = $0B"},
        "4392": {"synopsis":"One pixel row in both display files ($4000 and $6000)."},
        "4395": {"comment":"The second display file, $2000 on"},
        "4402": {"comment":"Back to the first display file"},
        "4406": {"comment":"The next pixel row down"},
        "4408": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4410": {"comment":"MMU 3 back; no attributes"},
        "4415": {"synopsis":"One pixel row."},
        "4418": {"comment":"The next pixel row down"},
        "4420": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4422": {"comment":"The direction and DE kept"},
        "4424": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR for the line"},
        "4427": {"comment":"DE = the attributes moved into"},
        "4429": {"comment":"And for its source"},
        "4432": {"comment":"HL = the source's attributes"},
        "4435": {"comment":"The 32 attributes"},
        "4440": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "4441": {"synopsis":"The line done: B to the next, the way it goes."},
        "4442": {"comment":"Up or down?"},
        "4445": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "4448": {"synopsis":"Up: the next line is the one below."},
        "4449": {"synopsis":"The next, while C counts."},
        "4450": {"comment":"H = the direction again"},
        "4453": {"comment":"B = the line left free"},
        "4455": {"synopsis":"The freed line printed: the row at HL on line B (PRINT_ROW)."},
        "4456": {"comment":"C = the line"},
        "4457": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL on window line C, from column 0, in its syntax colours (ROW_COLOURED):\nATTR_T and MASK_T set for it, P_FLAG's temporary bits cleared, TV_FLAG bit 0 = $D5B7 bit 6\n(editing in the lower screen) and AT C, 0 (ROM 0's $07BA; in a Timex mode the window's top\nline added). With $D741 bit 2 set (no screen output) the row is only scanned. TV_FLAG is put\nback. From $0217, $09F1, $0AC4 and $0AEE.\nExit: carry; A = the syntax state at the row's end, B = its bits for the next row\n(ROW_COLOURED).","comment":"TV_FLAG kept"},
        "4460": {"comment":"Kept, put back at the end"},
        "4461": {"comment":"Screen output off: A = 4, a scan only"},
        "4466": {"comment":"Off: only scanned"},
        "4470": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "4471": {"comment":"The lower screen ($D5B7 bit 6)?"},
        "4476": {"comment":"Main screen"},
        "4480": {"comment":"Lower screen"},
        "4482": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG with bit 0 for the screen part."},
        "4485": {"comment":"MASK_T = 0"},
        "4488": {"comment":"MASK_T = 0"},
        "4490": {"comment":"P_FLAG: the temporary bits cleared"},
        "4495": {"comment":"AT C, 0"},
        "4496": {"comment":"B = the line, column 0"},
        "4502": {"comment":"ROM 0's $07BA: AT B, C"},
        "4505": {"comment":"BC, HL back"},
        "4507": {"comment":"A = 0: printed"},
        "4508": {"synopsis":"The row printed or scanned; TV_FLAG back."},
        "4511": {"comment":"H = TV_FLAG; the row back on the stack"},
        "4512": {"comment":"L = the state"},
        "4513": {"comment":"TV_FLAG back"},
        "4517": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "4521": {"synopsis":"The syntax state at the end of the row at HL: ROW_COLOURED with A = 4, nothing printed."},
        "4523": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL (when A bit 2 is clear; A = 4 only scans it), each cell in the colour\nof its part of the BASIC line, set as ATTR_T from a table in bank 7. The state is the row's\nflags byte (C, from HL + ($D73D)): bit 0 a line number may come, bit 2 in a dot command, bit\n5 at a statement's start, bit 6 the rest is a comment, bit 7 inside quotes.\n1. 0: a space in colour $D6DA.\n2. Codes 1-$1F, a keyword's characters (LINE_TO_ROWS): 6-$1F as 'A'-'Z', 1, 2, 4, 5 as ' ',\n   '!', '#', '$', in colour $D6EE; 3 is the R of REM and starts a comment.\n3. Digits at a line's start: colour $D6ED (the line number).\n4. At a statement's start '.' starts a dot command (colour $D6F5 up to ':') and ';' a\n   comment.\n5. Otherwise: a comment $D6F1, quotes and the text in them $D6F0, a letter $D6F2, a digit\n   $D6F3, anything else $D6F4; ':' starts a statement.\n6. Codes $80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN.\nExit: A = the state (bit 0 cleared), B = its bits 2, 5, 6 and 7 for a next row. Keeps HL,\nDE, C.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4526": {"comment":"D = the mode"},
        "4527": {"comment":"B = the columns"},
        "4531": {"comment":"C = the row's flags, the state"},
        "4534": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4536": {"synopsis":"One cell: a space?"},
        "4538": {"comment":"A space: classed with the text"},
        "4542": {"comment":"Below a space: a code"},
        "4544": {"comment":"A line number may come?"},
        "4546": {"comment":"No: the line number is over"},
        "4548": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "4551": {"comment":"Not a digit: the line number is over"},
        "4553": {"comment":"Statement start after it; colour $D6ED"},
        "4560": {"synopsis":"An empty cell: a space in colour $D6DA."},
        "4562": {"comment":"Colour $D6DA, normal"},
        "4567": {"synopsis":"Codes 1-$1F: a keyword's characters."},
        "4568": {"comment":"0: an empty cell"},
        "4570": {"comment":"No line number, no statement start now"},
        "4574": {"comment":"6-$1F: 'A'-'Z'"},
        "4576": {"comment":"6 or more?"},
        "4580": {"comment":"1-5: ' ', '!', 'R', '#', '$'"},
        "4582": {"comment":"3?"},
        "4586": {"comment":"3: REM's R, a comment follows"},
        "4590": {"synopsis":"In colour $D6EE, unless in a comment."},
        "4594": {"comment":"Keyword colour $D6EE"},
        "4599": {"synopsis":"A character from '!' up: the line number over."},
        "4601": {"comment":"At a statement's start?"},
        "4605": {"comment":"'.': a dot command"},
        "4609": {"comment":"'.': bit 2 kept, on"},
        "4611": {"comment":"Not a dot command"},
        "4613": {"comment":"';': a comment"},
        "4615": {"comment":"Not ';'"},
        "4619": {"synopsis":"Codes $80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN."},
        "4621": {"comment":"$80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN"},
        "4623": {"synopsis":"The statement started."},
        "4625": {"synopsis":"The colour by the state, then by the character.","comment":"A comment?"},
        "4627": {"comment":"Comment colour"},
        "4632": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "4634": {"comment":"String colour"},
        "4639": {"comment":"A quote itself: as a string"},
        "4641": {"comment":"A quote: string colour"},
        "4643": {"comment":"A dot command?"},
        "4645": {"comment":"Dot command colour"},
        "4648": {"comment":"In a dot command: ':' ends it"},
        "4650": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "4653": {"comment":"Letter colour"},
        "4658": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "4661": {"comment":"Digit colour"},
        "4666": {"comment":"Anything else"},
        "4669": {"synopsis":"':' starts a statement; a dot command ends.","comment":"':'?"},
        "4673": {"comment":"A statement starts; no dot command"},
        "4677": {"synopsis":"ATTR_T = the colour at DE; printed unless only scanning."},
        "4678": {"comment":"The colour from the table"},
        "4682": {"comment":"A = the character, D = the mode"},
        "4684": {"comment":"Printing?"},
        "4686": {"comment":"RST $28: printed"},
        "4689": {"synopsis":"A quote flips the in-quotes bit.","comment":"The cell's own character: a quote?"},
        "4694": {"comment":"The in-quotes bit flipped"},
        "4698": {"synopsis":"The next cell, up to the last column."},
        "4700": {"comment":"The next cell"},
        "4703": {"comment":"The state at the row's end"},
        "4706": {"comment":"HL, DE, BC back"},
        "4709": {"comment":"B = the bits a next row starts with"},
        "4713": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "4715": {"synopsis":"Codes $80 up: $80-$8F printed as they are; $90-$A9 as 'A'-'Z', $AA-$B1 as '1'-'8', $B2-$CB\nas 'a'-'z', $CC-$E5 as 'a'-'z' and $E6-$FF as 'A'-'Z' underlined (OVER 1, a backspace and\n'_'). In the standard mode ($5C7F bits 0-3 clear) they take colour $D6EF; codes $90 up are\nshown INVERSE 1 when that colour is $D6DA's, and always in the other modes."},
        "4716": {"comment":"Only scanning?"},
        "4718": {"comment":"Only scanning: no print"},
        "4720": {"comment":"The code kept"},
        "4721": {"comment":"The standard screen mode?"},
        "4726": {"comment":"Another mode: INVERSE for $90 up"},
        "4728": {"comment":"The normal colour"},
        "4732": {"comment":"And $D6EF, ATTR_T now"},
        "4738": {"comment":"Not the same: no inverse"},
        "4739": {"comment":"Different colours: no inverse"},
        "4741": {"synopsis":"Codes $90 up: INVERSE 1."},
        "4743": {"comment":"Codes $90 up?"},
        "4747": {"comment":"INVERSE 1"},
        "4753": {"synopsis":"The code turned into a character; E = 2 to underline it."},
        "4754": {"comment":"E = 1: not underlined"},
        "4756": {"comment":"$80-$8F as they are"},
        "4760": {"comment":"$90-$A9: 'A'-'Z'"},
        "4762": {"comment":"Below $AA?"},
        "4766": {"comment":"$AA up: E = 2"},
        "4767": {"comment":"$E6-$FF: 'A'-'Z', underlined"},
        "4769": {"comment":"$E6 up?"},
        "4773": {"comment":"$CC-$E5: 'a'-'z', underlined"},
        "4775": {"comment":"$CC up?"},
        "4779": {"comment":"$B2-$CB: 'a'-'z', not underlined"},
        "4782": {"comment":"$B2 up?"},
        "4786": {"comment":"$AA-$B1: '1'-'8'"},
        "4788": {"synopsis":"Printed, then INVERSE 0; when underlining, OVER 1, a backspace, '_', OVER 0."},
        "4789": {"comment":"INVERSE 0"},
        "4794": {"comment":"Underline?"},
        "4795": {"comment":"No underline: the next cell"},
        "4797": {"comment":"OVER 1"},
        "4800": {"comment":"E = 1"},
        "4802": {"comment":"Back over it, an underline"},
        "4805": {"comment":"'_'"},
        "4808": {"comment":"OVER 0"},
        "4813": {"comment":"The next cell"},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a digit '0'-'9'.\nChanges: F."},
        "4817": {"comment":"Above '9': no carry"},
        "4818": {"comment":"Below '0': no carry"},
        "4822": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter, A-Z or a-z.\nChanges: F."},
        "4825": {"comment":"Below 'A': no carry"},
        "4826": {"comment":"Below '[': carry"},
        "4829": {"comment":"Below 'a': no carry"},
        "4833": {"comment":"Below '{': carry"},
        "4836": {"synopsis":"Clears the window's screen lines, from its top line (IX + 1) to that + ($D73C), through ROM\n0's CLEAR_LINES. From $0337.\nChanges: as that routine."},
        "4839": {"comment":"C = the window's last line"},
        "4842": {"comment":"Plus the top line"},
        "4844": {"comment":"ROM 0's CLEAR_LINES: lines B to C"},
        "4848": {"synopsis":"B = 24 - B - (IX + 1): line B of the window as ROM 3 counts lines.\nChanges: A, B."},
        "4850": {"comment":"24 - B"},
        "4851": {"comment":"Less the window's top line"},
        "4856": {"synopsis":"HL = $5800 + 32 x B + C, the attribute address of line B, column C. Keeps BC.\nChanges: A, DE, HL."},
        "4857": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "4858": {"comment":"DE = 32 x B"},
        "4860": {"comment":"Three right shifts of B:E"},
        "4872": {"comment":"The attribute area"},
        "4875": {"comment":"Plus C"},
        "4876": {"comment":"Plus 32 x B"},
        "4880": {"synopsis":"Copies C bytes from HL to DE (LDIR, B = 0). Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, HL, DE kept"},
        "4883": {"comment":"BC = C"},
        "4887": {"comment":"All back"},
        "4891": {"synopsis":"Steps the editor's column count ($D73D) round COLUMN_CYCLE, 32 to 64 to 85 to 32\n(SET_COLUMNS), applies it (ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY) and restarts the editor (EDITOR_RESTART).\nNo reference to it was found in either page or in NextZXOS.","comment":"The column count now"},
        "4897": {"synopsis":"Up to the count now in the table."},
        "4901": {"comment":"L = the next count"},
        "4905": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY, then EDITOR_RESTART."},
        "4908": {"synopsis":"Restarts the editor with the mode in $D5EC: START_KEEP_EPPC ($0303), which stores it in\n$D5B8 and $D5EC, sets $D74E = E_PPC and clears bank 7 from $C000 (the row buffers) on."},
        "4911": {"synopsis":"$0303 with the mode in A (from MODE_TOGGLE)."},
        "4914": {"synopsis":"Moves the editor between the main and the lower screen: $D5B8 = 0, the columns applied (ROM\n0's COLUMNS_APPLY), the font set ($03BD), $D5B7 bit 6 flipped and bit 3 cleared; bit 6 set:\nthe lower screen ($041D); clear: the main screen ($042F, COLUMNS_APPLY again). The line in\n$D74E is set up (PREV_LINE_NUM) and the editor shown ($010C). From $0417 and NextZXOS ROM\n0's MENU_SCREEN ($11DA). Keeps IX.\nExit: carry."},
        "4916": {"comment":"The state byte $D5B8 = 0"},
        "4917": {"comment":"$D5B8 = 0"},
        "4920": {"comment":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY"},
        "4923": {"comment":"The font for the column count"},
        "4926": {"comment":"The lower screen flipped"},
        "4929": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped, bit 3 cleared"},
        "4935": {"comment":"Now the lower screen?"},
        "4939": {"comment":"To the lower screen"},
        "4942": {"comment":"On to the line"},
        "4944": {"synopsis":"To the main screen."},
        "4947": {"comment":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY"},
        "4950": {"synopsis":"The line in $D74E, if any, set up; the editor shown."},
        "4953": {"comment":"A line kept?"},
        "4958": {"comment":"The editor shown ($010C)"},
        "4961": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "4965": {"synopsis":"Sets the editor's column count: $D73D = L (H = 0) and $D73F = L + 3, the length of a row\n(its cells, a flags byte and a line number). From COLUMNS_NEXT and NextZXOS ROM 1's A3C_SET\n($0216, L = 32, 64 or 85).\nChanges: HL.","comment":"H = 0"},
        "4967": {"comment":"The column count"},
        "4970": {"comment":"The cells, flags and a number"},
        "4973": {"comment":"The row length"},
        "4977": {"synopsis":"COLUMNS_NEXT's table: each count followed by the next: 32, 64, 85, 32."},
        "4981": {"synopsis":"Restarts the editor (EDITOR_RESTART_A) in mode 8 when $D5EC is 0, otherwise in mode 0. No\nreference to it was found in either page or in NextZXOS."},
        "4985": {"comment":"8 when $D5EC = 0"},
        "4989": {"comment":"Otherwise mode 0"},
        "4992": {"synopsis":"With bank 0: NextZXOS ROM 1's CALL_DMMC_27A8 (the DivMMC memory's $27A8 with BC = HL = 10);\nbank 7; with no carry a beep ($03B9); E_PPC = 0; then COLUMNS_RESTART. No reference to it\nwas found in either page or in NextZXOS."},
        "4993": {"comment":"ROM 1's CALL_DMMC_27A8"},
        "4996": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "4997": {"comment":"No carry: a beep"},
        "5000": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "5003": {"comment":"E_PPC, the current line"},
        "5008": {"synopsis":"The alternate stack ($5B6A) moved to UDG - 1; with bank 0, NextZXOS ROM 1's CLEAR_CHECK\n($3485); bank 7; then COLUMNS_RESTART. No reference to it was found in either page or in\nNextZXOS.","comment":"UDG - 1"},
        "5013": {"comment":"The alternate stack's top"},
        "5017": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5018": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_CHECK"},
        "5021": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5024": {"synopsis":"Key $11 (EDIT_KEY_TABLE; NextZXOS ROM 0's LINEIN_KEY_11 at $2A70 too): FLAGS2 ($5C6A) bit 7\nflipped.\nExit: A = 0, carry.","comment":"FLAGS2"},
        "5027": {"synopsis":"Flips bit 7 of (HL).\nExit: A = 0, carry.","comment":"Bit 7"},
        "5031": {"comment":"A = 0, carry"},
        "5034": {"synopsis":"Key $12 (EDIT_KEY_TABLE): TV_FLAG bit 7 flipped (with it set, EXPAND_NEXT expands keywords\ninside quotes too), then EDITOR_RESTART.","comment":"TV_FLAG"},
        "5037": {"comment":"Bit 7 flipped"},
        "5043": {"synopsis":"The editor's key table, read by $039F (through $00E4): for each key a code and the address\nof its routine (a word), ended by $FF: $0B $05E4, $0A $0605, $08 $0627, $09 $0633, $0C\n$049B, $0D $04C2, $1F $05A0, $1E $0576, $04 $052A, $05 $0535, $1A $04FE, $01 $0525, $1D\n$05D7, $00 $05CA, $18 $0488, $1C $0BBE, $1B $0B5F, $10 $0C16, $03 $0BE4, $11 KEY_11, $12\nKEY_12, $19 $040F, $07 $03F7."},
        "5113": {"synopsis":"PREV_LINE_START for the line before line HL.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone. From NextZXOS ROM 1's STORE_LINE_NEW ($0D6D) too."},
        "5116": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5117": {"comment":"None: HL = 0, no carry"},
        "5121": {"synopsis":"NEXT_LINE_START for the line after line HL (the first line for HL = 0).\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone."},
        "5124": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5125": {"comment":"None: HL = 0, no carry"},
        "5129": {"synopsis":"The next character of the program line being expanded (set up by NEXT_LINE_START,\nPREV_LINE_START or LINE_START_NUM):\n1. While a text is pending at ($D765) (a line number, a keyword's text): its next character;\n   $D761 = $FF for a space with bit 7 (a keyword's last), else 0; $D762 = 0; $D765 = 0 after\n   the last (bit 7). A letter, '#' or '$' gives B = 1 (a keyword's character); anything else\n   B = the byte.\n2. Otherwise the next byte of the line at ($D763), with bank 0: a number's hidden form and a\n   colour code's argument are passed over; a quote flips $D762 bit 0 (inside quotes).\n3. Codes $A5 up (outside quotes, or with TV_FLAG bit 7 set) put ROM 3's keyword text in the\n   buffer (KEYWORD_TEXT at $D772 with ROM 3, its table from $0096), codes $81-$A4 this ROM's\n   (NEXT_KEYWORDS); then step 1. $D760 = the last byte.\n4. Any other byte: $D761 = 0, B = it; ENTER ends the expansion ($D763 = 0).\nExit: carry and A = the character; no carry when nothing is left.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A text pending?"},
        "5136": {"comment":"Its next character"},
        "5137": {"comment":"HL = the next one"},
        "5138": {"comment":"A keyword's last space?"},
        "5140": {"comment":"B = the character as stored"},
        "5145": {"comment":"$FF: a keyword's last space"},
        "5146": {"synopsis":"$D761 = 0, or $FF after a keyword's last space."},
        "5149": {"comment":"Not inside quotes"},
        "5150": {"comment":"$D762 = 0"},
        "5153": {"comment":"The last character (bit 7)?"},
        "5157": {"comment":"HL = 0: the text done"},
        "5159": {"synopsis":"$D765 = the next character, or 0 after the last."},
        "5162": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5163": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "5165": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "5169": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "5173": {"comment":"'$'? Otherwise carry, B = the byte"},
        "5177": {"synopsis":"B = 1: a keyword's character; carry."},
        "5181": {"synopsis":"Nothing pending: the next byte of the line, if any."},
        "5184": {"comment":"Any line left?"},
        "5186": {"comment":"No: no carry"},
        "5187": {"comment":"Bank 0: the program"},
        "5188": {"synopsis":"A = the byte; a number's hidden form passed over."},
        "5190": {"comment":"A number's hidden form?"},
        "5194": {"comment":"The five bytes after $0E"},
        "5196": {"comment":"Five bytes passed"},
        "5200": {"synopsis":"A colour code ($10-$15): its argument passed over."},
        "5202": {"comment":"Below $10: a character"},
        "5204": {"comment":"$16 up: a character"},
        "5208": {"comment":"$10-$15: its argument passed"},
        "5211": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; $D763 on."},
        "5212": {"comment":"The place in the line"},
        "5215": {"comment":"HL = the quote flag"},
        "5218": {"comment":"A quote flips it"},
        "5222": {"comment":"The byte kept"},
        "5224": {"comment":"Bit 0 flipped: inside quotes"},
        "5227": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "5228": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 7 clear and inside quotes: the byte as it is.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 7: keywords in quotes too"},
        "5234": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "5236": {"comment":"Yes: the byte as it is"},
        "5238": {"synopsis":"$D760 = the byte; a keyword's code?"},
        "5241": {"comment":"$A5 up?"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Codes $A5 up: ROM 3's keyword table"},
        "5247": {"comment":"ROM 3's table from RND"},
        "5250": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT at $D772 with ROM 3"},
        "5253": {"comment":"Its text given now"},
        "5255": {"synopsis":"Codes $81-$A4: this ROM's NEXT_KEYWORDS."},
        "5257": {"comment":"Below $81: a character"},
        "5259": {"comment":"The word's number"},
        "5264": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT at $D772 with this ROM"},
        "5267": {"comment":"Its text given now"},
        "5270": {"synopsis":"Any other byte: $D761 = 0, B = it; ENTER ends the expansion."},
        "5271": {"comment":"$D761 = 0"},
        "5275": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "5280": {"comment":"$D763 = 0: the line done"},
        "5285": {"synopsis":"Carry: A is a character."},
        "5286": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "5287": {"synopsis":"IDE_TOKENISER ($01D8, as documented), reached from NextZXOS ROM 2's IDE_TOKENISER ($1093,\nthrough $3E18): converts a BASIC line between plain text and tokens; C = the 8K bank of the\ntext buffer, HL = its offset ($0000-$1FFF), seen at $2000-$3FFF through MMU 1 ($D7F6 the\nbank, $D7F8 the address).\n1. B = 0: the text, ended by ENTER, is tokenised at E_LINE (TOKENISE_TEXT).\n2. B = 1: the tokenised line at DE is expanded (EXPAND_INIT, $D763 = DE, no space first) and\n   each character written to the buffer through MMU 1 (MMU 1 = $FF, the ROM, after each); at\n   the 8K page's end the place stops moving.\nExit: carry; for B = 1, HL = the offset after the text. Bank 0 on exit.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5288": {"comment":"C = the buffer's bank"},
        "5292": {"comment":"Its address through MMU 1"},
        "5294": {"comment":"$D7F8 = the buffer's address"},
        "5297": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5298": {"comment":"B = 0: tokenise"},
        "5302": {"comment":"Detokenise: bank 7"},
        "5303": {"comment":"DE = the tokenised line"},
        "5304": {"comment":"The expansion reset"},
        "5307": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "5308": {"comment":"The line to expand"},
        "5311": {"comment":"$D761 = $FF: no space first"},
        "5314": {"comment":"$D761 = $FF, $D762 = 0"},
        "5317": {"synopsis":"The next character, until none is left."},
        "5320": {"comment":"HL = the place in the buffer"},
        "5323": {"comment":"None left: done"},
        "5325": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "5326": {"comment":"The buffer's bank in MMU 1"},
        "5332": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5334": {"comment":"The ROM back in MMU 1"},
        "5338": {"comment":"At the 8K page's end?"},
        "5344": {"comment":"No: the place moves on"},
        "5347": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5349": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; HL = the offset; carry."},
        "5350": {"comment":"The offset in the bank"},
        "5354": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE in mode 1 ($D7EE = 1), from $085E: the line is walked, not written, to find X_PTR's\nplace in the text.","comment":"Mode 1: walked"},
        "5358": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE in mode 0 ($D7EE = 0), from $0817: the line is written.","comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "5360": {"synopsis":"Turns the line the editor holds, read character by character (TOK_GET_CHAR), into a BASIC\nline at E_LINE:\n1. The work space cleared with bank 0: ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS (A = 0) or CLEAR_WS (A not 0),\n   through ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC.\n2. $D7EE = D (the mode), $D7EC = SP, $D7F7 = A (where the characters come from: 0 the\n   editor's rows, 1 the banked buffer of IDE_TOKENISER, $FF memory), $D7EA = E_LINE (the\n   place written), $D7EF-$D7F5 cleared; the RAM routines copied (RAM_ROUTINES).\n3. Each character goes through a small state machine in $D7F1: letters, '#' and '$' are\n   collected into a word at $D7E1 (TOK_BUF_ADD), which a following character looks up as a\n   keyword (KEYWORD_LOOKUP); a word that is not one is written as text (TOK_FLUSH), one that\n   holds a space is split there (TOK_SPLIT).\n4. Characters are written by TOK_OUT; ENTER ends the line.\nExit: no carry at the end of the line (mode 0); in mode 1, reaching X_PTR returns from here\nwith carry and BC = the characters before it (TOK_WRITE). Bank 7.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5361": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE with A on entry: 0 or not 0 as above.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "5367": {"comment":"A = 0: ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS instead"},
        "5370": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; ROM 3's routine at BC (ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC); bank 7."},
        "5371": {"comment":"ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC"},
        "5374": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5375": {"comment":"B = the mode"},
        "5376": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "5380": {"synopsis":"The tokenizer's state set: A = the source, B = the mode. From TOKENISE_MEM too.","comment":"HL = the mode"},
        "5383": {"comment":"$D7EE = the mode"},
        "5384": {"comment":"SP kept for a return from mode 1"},
        "5388": {"comment":"$D7F7 = the source"},
        "5391": {"comment":"The place written: E_LINE"},
        "5395": {"comment":"7 bytes: $D7EF-$D7F5"},
        "5397": {"synopsis":"$D7EF-$D7F5 cleared."},
        "5402": {"comment":"The RAM routines to $D772"},
        "5405": {"synopsis":"The next character: $D7F3 counted, B = it, C = its class (TOK_GET_CHAR).","comment":"TOK_GET_CHAR: B, C"},
        "5408": {"synopsis":"State 1 ($D7F1): in a word?"},
        "5411": {"comment":"In a word?"},
        "5413": {"comment":"State 1"},
        "5415": {"comment":"Another state: written as it is"},
        "5416": {"comment":"Not state 0"},
        "5418": {"synopsis":"State 0: a letter?"},
        "5420": {"comment":"Not a letter: written"},
        "5422": {"synopsis":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD): state 1."},
        "5425": {"comment":"Full"},
        "5427": {"comment":"State 1: in a word"},
        "5432": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5434": {"synopsis":"The buffer full: split at a space (TOK_SPLIT), or written as text (TOK_FLUSH) and the rest\nof the word passed ($D7F1 bit 4)."},
        "5437": {"comment":"Split: on with the character"},
        "5442": {"comment":"Bit 4: the rest of the word as text"},
        "5444": {"comment":"On with the character"},
        "5446": {"synopsis":"B written (TOK_OUT); a character other than a letter ends a passed word. At ENTER in mode 0,\nTOKENIZE ends with no carry.","comment":"A letter?"},
        "5448": {"comment":"No: the word passing ends"},
        "5455": {"comment":"The line's end: no carry"},
        "5456": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5458": {"synopsis":"State 1: a letter, '#' or '$' goes into the buffer.","comment":"A letter, '#' or '$'?"},
        "5460": {"comment":"Yes: into the buffer"},
        "5462": {"synopsis":"The word ended: looked up (KEYWORD_LOOKUP); a keyword's token written (TOK_OUT), the buffer\nemptied, and the character taken again.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "5466": {"comment":"Not a keyword"},
        "5468": {"comment":"The token written"},
        "5471": {"comment":"The buffer emptied"},
        "5474": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "5477": {"synopsis":"Not a keyword: split at a space (TOK_SPLIT) and the rest looked up again; a space goes into\nthe buffer."},
        "5481": {"comment":"No space in the word"},
        "5483": {"comment":"Still in a word?"},
        "5486": {"comment":"Still a word?"},
        "5489": {"comment":"State 0: the character again"},
        "5491": {"synopsis":"A space?","comment":"A space?"},
        "5493": {"comment":"Anything else"},
        "5495": {"comment":"The space into the buffer"},
        "5498": {"comment":"Full"},
        "5500": {"comment":"The buffer holds a space"},
        "5505": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5507": {"synopsis":"Anything else: the buffer written as text (TOK_FLUSH); the character taken again."},
        "5510": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "5512": {"synopsis":"With a space in the word buffer ($D7F0 not 0): the characters before it written as text\n(TOK_OUT) and the rest moved to the buffer's start ($D7EF = its length); a buffer that ends\nwith its space ($A0) is emptied.\nExit: carry when done; no carry, nothing done, when $D7F0 is 0. Keeps BC.","comment":"A space in the buffer?"},
        "5516": {"comment":"No: no carry"},
        "5518": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5521": {"synopsis":"One character written; the space reached?","comment":"The place kept"},
        "5528": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "5529": {"comment":"The character written"},
        "5531": {"comment":"The end ($A0)?"},
        "5535": {"comment":"The space?"},
        "5537": {"comment":"On to the space"},
        "5539": {"comment":"The rest to the buffer's start"},
        "5542": {"comment":"A counts the characters moved"},
        "5543": {"synopsis":"One character moved, up to the one with bit 7."},
        "5544": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "5546": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "5550": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5551": {"comment":"$D7EF = the count"},
        "5553": {"synopsis":"BC back; the buffer emptied."},
        "5554": {"synopsis":"State bit 0 cleared; the buffer empty.","comment":"The state"},
        "5557": {"comment":"Not in a word"},
        "5559": {"comment":"Length 0"},
        "5560": {"synopsis":"$D7EF = A, the length; no space in it ($D7F0 = 0)."},
        "5563": {"comment":"No space in it"},
        "5567": {"synopsis":"$D7F1 bit 4 cleared: no word passed as text.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The state"},
        "5570": {"comment":"Not passing a word"},
        "5574": {"synopsis":"Writes the word buffer as text (TOK_OUT for each character, up to the one with bit 7) and\nempties it (TOK_BUF_RESET). Keeps BC.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "5575": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5578": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"The character"},
        "5586": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "5591": {"comment":"The buffer emptied"},
        "5593": {"synopsis":"The next character in B and its class in C, $D7F3 counted: from the banked buffer\n(TOK_GET_BANK) when $D7F7 is 1, from the editor's rows (ROWS_READ_CHAR, $08AE) when 0, from\nmemory (TOK_GET_MEM) when $FF. Class 6 a letter, 2 '#' or '$', 3 a space, 1 anything else.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"One more character read"},
        "5600": {"comment":"Where from?"},
        "5603": {"comment":"$FF: memory"},
        "5607": {"comment":"1: the banked buffer"},
        "5610": {"comment":"0: the editor's rows (ROWS_READ_CHAR, $08AE)"},
        "5613": {"synopsis":"B = the character; its class."},
        "5614": {"comment":"Class 1 for a start"},
        "5616": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "5620": {"comment":"Lower case for the test"},
        "5622": {"comment":"Not a letter: 1"},
        "5625": {"comment":"Not a letter: 1"},
        "5628": {"comment":"A letter"},
        "5631": {"synopsis":"Below 'A': '#' or '$' 2, a space 3, else 1.","comment":"2"},
        "5632": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "5635": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "5638": {"comment":"3"},
        "5639": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "5642": {"comment":"Else 1"},
        "5645": {"synopsis":"From memory: ($D7FA) characters at ($D7F8), read with bank 0; ENTER when none are left.","comment":"Characters left"},
        "5650": {"comment":"None: ENTER"},
        "5654": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "5658": {"comment":"The place"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5662": {"comment":"The character"},
        "5664": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5665": {"comment":"The place moved on"},
        "5668": {"comment":"Classed"},
        "5670": {"synopsis":"Adds character B to the word buffer ($D7E1, up to 9 characters, $D7EF the length), the last\none marked with bit 7.\nExit: carry; no carry (Z) when it is full.","comment":"Full?"},
        "5673": {"comment":"Full: Z, no carry"},
        "5676": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5679": {"comment":"HL = the next place"},
        "5681": {"comment":"The first character?"},
        "5684": {"comment":"Bit 7 off the one before"},
        "5688": {"synopsis":"B stored with bit 7 set; the length + 1."},
        "5689": {"comment":"The last now"},
        "5691": {"comment":"One more"},
        "5697": {"synopsis":"Writes A, joining a '<' or '>' with the character after it: either is held in $D7F5; then <<\ngives $8C, <= $C7, <> $C9, >> $8D, >= $C8, and anything else writes the held one first.\nInside quotes or a comment ($D7F1 bits 1 and 3) A goes straight on (TOK_PUT); THEN ($CB) or\n':' ends a dot command and starts a statement ($D7F2 bit 2 cleared).\nExit: carry, except at the line's end (TOK_PUT).","comment":"The state"},
        "5700": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "5702": {"comment":"Yes: straight on"},
        "5704": {"comment":"In a comment?"},
        "5706": {"comment":"Yes: straight on"},
        "5708": {"comment":"THEN or ':': a new statement"},
        "5710": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "5712": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "5714": {"comment":"No"},
        "5716": {"synopsis":"The dot command over; written; a statement starts.","comment":"Not a dot command now"},
        "5721": {"comment":"At a statement's start"},
        "5727": {"synopsis":"Is a '<' or '>' held?","comment":"B = the character"},
        "5728": {"comment":"One held?"},
        "5733": {"comment":"Yes: a pair?"},
        "5735": {"comment":"None: hold a '>' or '<'"},
        "5736": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5740": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "5742": {"comment":"Neither: written"},
        "5744": {"synopsis":"Held; carry.","comment":"$D7F5 = it"},
        "5747": {"synopsis":"One is held: $D7F5 = 0; was it '<'?","comment":"Nothing held now"},
        "5749": {"comment":"'>' held?"},
        "5751": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5754": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5756": {"comment":"<>"},
        "5760": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "5762": {"comment":"<="},
        "5766": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "5768": {"comment":"<<"},
        "5772": {"comment":"Else '<' first"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"The held character written first, then A.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "5775": {"comment":"The held one written"},
        "5779": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "5782": {"synopsis":"'>' held: then '=' gives >=, '>' >>.","comment":"'='?"},
        "5784": {"comment":">="},
        "5788": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "5790": {"comment":"Else '>' first"},
        "5794": {"comment":">>"},
        "5796": {"synopsis":"A = B, the pair's token."},
        "5797": {"synopsis":"Writes A, keeping the state: ENTER ends the line (in mode 1 a return from TOKENIZE,\nTOK_WRITE_FOUND; in mode 0 a held space written, then no carry); a quote flips $D7F1 bit 1;\nat a statement's start ';' makes $D7F1 8 (a comment), '.' 4 (a dot command; not when $D5B8\nis 4), and REM ($EA) sets $D7F2 bit 4. Everything else through TOK_SPACING.\nExit: carry.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "5801": {"comment":"ENTER: mode 1?"},
        "5804": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "5805": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "5809": {"comment":"Mode 1: out of TOKENIZE"},
        "5812": {"comment":"A space held: written"},
        "5815": {"comment":"A space held?"},
        "5822": {"comment":"No carry: the line done"},
        "5824": {"synopsis":"B = A; a quote?"},
        "5825": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "5829": {"comment":"Past a statement's start?"},
        "5832": {"comment":"Bit 2: the statement started"},
        "5834": {"comment":"Yes: written"},
        "5836": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "5838": {"comment":"Bit 4 then"},
        "5840": {"comment":"';': a comment"},
        "5842": {"comment":"State 8"},
        "5844": {"comment":"'.': a dot command"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Not '.'"},
        "5848": {"comment":"Unless the state byte is 4"},
        "5851": {"comment":"A = 4: state 4"},
        "5854": {"comment":"Not 4: a dot command"},
        "5856": {"synopsis":"Written (TOK_SPACING); carry."},
        "5862": {"synopsis":"REM: $D7F2 bit 4."},
        "5864": {"comment":"Written"},
        "5866": {"synopsis":"';': state 8."},
        "5868": {"synopsis":"$D7F1 = A."},
        "5871": {"comment":"Written"},
        "5873": {"synopsis":"A quote: $D7F1 bit 1 flipped."},
        "5876": {"comment":"Bit 1 flipped"},
        "5878": {"comment":"Stored, written"},
        "5880": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_WRITE), dropping the spaces around keywords, with the flags in $D7F2 (bit 0 a\nkeyword was the last, bit 1 a space held, bit 2 the statement has started, bit 3 something\nwritten): a space after a keyword is dropped, the line's first space too; otherwise a space\nis held (bit 1) and one more written; a keyword ($81 up, outside quotes, comments and dot\ncommands) drops a held space, and after REM makes the state a comment; any other character\nwrites a held space first. A character other than a digit sets bits 2 and 3.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, B.","comment":"E = the character"},
        "5881": {"comment":"D = the flags"},
        "5886": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "5888": {"comment":"Not a space"},
        "5890": {"comment":"After a keyword: dropped"},
        "5892": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared; dropped"},
        "5894": {"comment":"One held: this one written"},
        "5896": {"comment":"Bit 1: this one written"},
        "5898": {"comment":"Something written: held"},
        "5900": {"comment":"Bit 3: hold it"},
        "5902": {"comment":"At the line's start: bit 3 only"},
        "5903": {"comment":"The space dropped"},
        "5907": {"synopsis":"Bit 1: a space held."},
        "5908": {"comment":"Held"},
        "5910": {"synopsis":"$D7F2 = A.","comment":"The flags stored"},
        "5914": {"synopsis":"E written (TOK_WRITE).","comment":"A = the character"},
        "5917": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 cleared."},
        "5918": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "5920": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5922": {"synopsis":"Not a space: a digit?","comment":"A digit?"},
        "5928": {"comment":"Yes: the flags as they are"},
        "5930": {"synopsis":"Not a digit: bits 2 and 3 set."},
        "5932": {"comment":"Something written"},
        "5934": {"synopsis":"A keyword ($81 up)?","comment":"A keyword?"},
        "5936": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5938": {"synopsis":"A held space written first, then the character; bits 0 and 1 cleared.","comment":"A space held?"},
        "5941": {"comment":"Written first"},
        "5947": {"comment":"None held now"},
        "5949": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "5952": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "5954": {"synopsis":"A keyword, outside quotes, comments and dot commands?","comment":"The state"},
        "5958": {"comment":"Quotes, a dot command or a comment?"},
        "5960": {"comment":"Yes: as text"},
        "5962": {"comment":"After REM?"},
        "5967": {"comment":"Then the state a comment"},
        "5969": {"synopsis":"A held space dropped, bit 0 set; written."},
        "5971": {"comment":"A keyword the last"},
        "5973": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5976": {"comment":"Written"},
        "5978": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the place in $D7EA and moves it on. Mode 0 ($D7EE = 0): one byte of room made\nthere with bank 0 (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE) and A stored. Mode 1: the place moves past the\nline's byte (and a number's hidden form) instead; on reaching X_PTR, BC = the characters\nread less those still in the word buffer, SP = $D7EC and a return from TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "5979": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "5982": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "5986": {"comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "5988": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "5989": {"comment":"X_PTR reached?"},
        "5994": {"comment":"No"},
        "5996": {"comment":"BC = $D7F3 - $D7EF"},
        "5999": {"comment":"DE = the buffer's length"},
        "6002": {"comment":"Less the characters read"},
        "6007": {"comment":"BC = the place's count"},
        "6010": {"synopsis":"SP back: out of TOKENIZE.","comment":"Out of TOKENIZE"},
        "6015": {"synopsis":"Mode 1: past the byte, with bank 0; past a hidden number's six bytes.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6016": {"comment":"Past the byte"},
        "6018": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "6022": {"comment":"Its marker and five bytes"},
        "6028": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: room for one byte at HL, then A stored there.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6029": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "6030": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE"},
        "6033": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6034": {"comment":"Stored in the new byte"},
        "6035": {"comment":"The next place"},
        "6036": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; $D7EA = the next place.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6037": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6042": {"synopsis":"Looks the word in the buffer at $D7E1 up as a keyword, letters in either case, unless a word\nis being passed as text ($D7F1 bit 4):\n1. In ROM 3's table from RND's entry ($0096), through WORD_FIND at $D7B0 with ROM 3: codes\n   $A5 up.\n2. In NEXT_KEYWORDS (codes $D0 up for WORD_FIND): its first 36 words give $81-$A4; the rest\n   are other spellings, their tokens from ALIAS_TOKENS; one ending in '$' writes the token\n   (TOK_OUT) and gives '$'.\nExit: carry and A = the token (or '$'); no carry when not found or passing.","comment":"The state"},
        "6045": {"comment":"Passing a word?"},
        "6047": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "6048": {"comment":"ROM 3's keywords from RND, code $A5"},
        "6053": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORD_FIND at $D7B0"},
        "6056": {"comment":"Found: carry, A = the token"},
        "6057": {"comment":"This ROM's, from code $D0"},
        "6062": {"comment":"WORD_FIND, this ROM's"},
        "6065": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "6066": {"comment":"$F4 up: another spelling"},
        "6068": {"comment":"$D0-$F3: a token"},
        "6070": {"comment":"BC = its number from $F4"},
        "6073": {"comment":"Its last character"},
        "6075": {"comment":"Its token from ALIAS_TOKENS"},
        "6078": {"comment":"HL = its token"},
        "6079": {"comment":"Ending in '$'?"},
        "6081": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "6082": {"comment":"No '$'"},
        "6084": {"comment":"The token written; then '$'"},
        "6087": {"comment":"Then '$'"},
        "6089": {"synopsis":"Carry: found."},
        "6091": {"synopsis":"$D0-$F3: tokens $81-$A4.","comment":"A = the token"},
        "6095": {"synopsis":"Tokenises BC characters at DE (read with bank 0, TOK_GET_MEM) into a line at E_LINE\n(TOKENIZE_GO with A = $FF, mode 0).\nExit: BC = ($D7EA), the place written, less STKBOT - 1 as it was on entry; bank 0. No\nreference to it was found in this page or in NextZXOS (page 1 has its own $17CF).","comment":"STKBOT - 1 kept"},
        "6098": {"comment":"STKBOT - 1"},
        "6100": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "6101": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6102": {"comment":"The text and its length"},
        "6105": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "6109": {"comment":"From memory, mode 0"},
        "6111": {"comment":"Mode 0"},
        "6116": {"comment":"BC = the end less it"},
        "6119": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6120": {"comment":"DE = STKBOT - 1"},
        "6122": {"comment":"BC = the end less it"},
        "6127": {"synopsis":"IDE_TOKENISER with B = 0: the work space cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_WS), an ENTER put at E_LINE\n(ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE), the text in the banked buffer tokenised before it (TOKENIZE_RUN,\nmode 0), then NextZXOS ROM 1's code at $0A05 (inside LINE_ENTER) run with HL = $09FB and the\nDivMMC memory's byte at $32FF set to 0 round it (DMMC_BYTE_SWAP). With no report (ERR_NR bit\n7 set) and at most $04FB characters: HL = E_LINE, BC = the line's length (TOKAPI_LENGTH),\nNZ. Otherwise the text is walked again to X_PTR, the report's place (mode 1): Z, DE = the\ncount returned less 1.\nExit: carry; bank 0.","comment":"The buffer's address kept"},
        "6128": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "6131": {"comment":"The workspace's HL kept, below it"},
        "6133": {"comment":"An ENTER at E_LINE"},
        "6136": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM_ONE"},
        "6139": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "6142": {"comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "6147": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's address"},
        "6148": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6149": {"comment":"Its address again"},
        "6152": {"comment":"The DivMMC byte $32FF = 0, B = it"},
        "6156": {"comment":"The old byte kept"},
        "6157": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6158": {"comment":"ROM 1's $0A05: the line checked"},
        "6161": {"comment":"ROM 1's $0A05"},
        "6164": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6165": {"comment":"The DivMMC byte back"},
        "6169": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "6173": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6174": {"comment":"DE = the workspace's HL kept"},
        "6175": {"comment":"ERR_NR bit 7: no report?"},
        "6179": {"comment":"No report"},
        "6181": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "6182": {"comment":"Mode 1: to the report's place"},
        "6184": {"comment":"TOKENIZE_RUN in mode 1"},
        "6187": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "6188": {"synopsis":"Z: DE = the characters before the error; the work space cleared.","comment":"The count less 1"},
        "6193": {"comment":"DE = the count less 1"},
        "6194": {"comment":"Z"},
        "6197": {"synopsis":"No report: more than $04FB characters is an error too.","comment":"The limit"},
        "6201": {"comment":"More characters than that?"},
        "6203": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "6205": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS; BC = its HL now less DE (its HL at the start, kept on the stack), the\nline's length; HL = E_LINE; carry."},
        "6208": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6213": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6218": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE with A = 1 (the banked buffer, its work space cleared by CLEAR_WS) and mode D, bank\n7 round it; bank 0 on exit.","comment":"The banked buffer"},
        "6220": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6224": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6226": {"synopsis":"Swaps A with the DivMMC memory's byte at $32FF: DMMC_SWAP_CODE copied to $D7B0 and run there\n(DivMMC memory paged in by port $E3 = $80 while it reads and writes).\nExit: B = the old byte, A = 0. From NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_OWN ($0DBA) too.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6229": {"comment":"To $D7B0"},
        "6232": {"comment":"Run there on the RET"},
        "6238": {"comment":"The byte's address in that memory"},
        "6241": {"comment":"C = the new byte"},
        "6242": {"comment":"A = $80 for port $E3"},
        "6244": {"comment":"DMMC_SWAP_CODE at $D7B0"},
        "6245": {"synopsis":"Run at $D7B0 (DMMC_BYTE_SWAP): port $E3 = A ($80, the DivMMC memory paged in), B = (HL),\n(HL) = C, port $E3 = 0.","comment":"The DivMMC memory paged in"},
        "6247": {"comment":"B = the old byte"},
        "6248": {"comment":"The new one written"},
        "6249": {"comment":"Paged out"},
        "6253": {"synopsis":"The next character from the banked buffer: ($D7F8) with the bank in $D7F6 paged into MMU 1,\nthen the ROM back (MMU 1 = $FF); $D7F8 moved on.\nExit: NZ.","comment":"The place"},
        "6256": {"comment":"The buffer's bank"},
        "6259": {"comment":"In MMU 1"},
        "6262": {"comment":"The character"},
        "6264": {"comment":"The ROM back"},
        "6268": {"comment":"The place moved on"},
        "6271": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "6273": {"synopsis":"Resets the expansion of a line ($D763, the place in the program, and $D765, the place in a\ntext, both 0), then RAM_ROUTINES.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No text pending"},
        "6276": {"comment":"No line"},
        "6282": {"synopsis":"Copies KEYWORD_TEXT and WORD_FIND ($1896-$18FA, 101 bytes) to $D772-$D7D6, where they run\nwith ROM 3 or this ROM paged in.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT and WORD_FIND"},
        "6285": {"comment":"To $D772"},
        "6288": {"comment":"101 bytes"},
        "6294": {"synopsis":"Run at $D772: puts the text of the A-th string of the table at DE (each ended by bit 7) in\nthe buffer at $D767 for EXPAND_NEXT ($D765 = $D767): a space first when the word starts with\na letter and $D761 bit 0 is clear, then the string, then a space ($A0, the last) unless it\nends with '<', '=' or '>' (bit 7 then on its last character). $D761 = 0.\nExit: HL past the buffer's text.","comment":"B = the strings to pass over"},
        "6295": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6296": {"synopsis":"Any more to pass over?"},
        "6298": {"synopsis":"Up to the end of this string (bit 7)."},
        "6299": {"comment":"Up to the one with bit 7"},
        "6304": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "6307": {"synopsis":"The string reached: a space first?","comment":"$D761"},
        "6310": {"comment":"Bit 0: no space first"},
        "6312": {"comment":"$D761 = 0"},
        "6314": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "6317": {"comment":"Its text given first"},
        "6320": {"comment":"No space first"},
        "6322": {"comment":"A letter first?"},
        "6327": {"comment":"A space first"},
        "6331": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the one with bit 7.","comment":"A character"},
        "6333": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "6336": {"comment":"The last?"},
        "6340": {"comment":"The last character"},
        "6343": {"comment":"'<', '=' or '>'?"},
        "6349": {"comment":"Yes: no space after"},
        "6350": {"synopsis":"Its last character without bit 7, then $A0.","comment":"Its bit 7 off"},
        "6353": {"comment":"Then a space with bit 7"},
        "6356": {"synopsis":"Run at $D7B0: compares the word at $D7E1 (its last character with bit 7 set) with the\nstrings at HL, each ended by bit 7, B the code of the first: lower-case letters in the word\ncount as capitals.\nExit: carry, A = B = the code of the one that matches, HL past it; no carry when none does\nbefore B passes $FF.","comment":"The word"},
        "6359": {"synopsis":"The word's next character, a letter as a capital.","comment":"The word's character"},
        "6362": {"comment":"Lower case?"},
        "6367": {"comment":"As a capital"},
        "6369": {"synopsis":"The same as the string's?","comment":"The same as the string's?"},
        "6370": {"comment":"No"},
        "6372": {"comment":"Both moved on"},
        "6374": {"comment":"The word's last?"},
        "6378": {"comment":"Matched: carry"},
        "6381": {"synopsis":"No match: the next string's code; past $FF, none found.","comment":"The next code"},
        "6382": {"comment":"Past $FF: none"},
        "6384": {"synopsis":"Past the end of this string.","comment":"To the end of this string"},
        "6390": {"comment":"Compared again"},
        "6392": {"synopsis":"None found: no carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "6393": {"synopsis":"A = B.","comment":"A = the code"},
        "6395": {"synopsis":"NextBASIC's own keywords, each ended by bit 7: tokens $81-$A4, TIME, PRIVATE, IF, ENDIF,\nEXIT, REF, PEEK$, REG, DPOKE, DPEEK, MOD, <<, >>, UNTIL, ERROR, ON, DEFPROC, ENDPROC, PROC,\nLOCAL, DRIVER, WHILE, REPEAT, ELSE, REMOUNT, BANK, TILE, LAYER, PALETTE, SPRITE, PWD, CD,\nMKDIR, RMDIR, SPECTRUM, PLAY; then 12 other spellings for ALIAS_TOKENS: LS, DIR, GOTO,\nGOSUB, DEFFN, OPEN#, CLOSE#, RAND, CONT, ERROR$, TIME$, USR$. Read by EXPAND_NEXT (through\nKEYWORD_TEXT, code - $81) and KEYWORD_LOOKUP (WORD_FIND, B = $D0 for the first)."},
        "6614": {"synopsis":"The tokens of NEXT_KEYWORDS' last 12 words, read by KEYWORD_LOOKUP: LS and DIR $CF (CAT),\nGOTO $EC, GOSUB $ED, DEFFN $CE, OPEN# $D3, CLOSE# $D4, RAND $F9, CONT $E8, ERROR$ $8F, TIME$\n$81 and USR$ $C0 (the last three followed by '$')."},
        "6626": {"synopsis":"Prints program lines through RST $28, from the line at HL in bank ($5B65) on (NextZXOS ROM\n1's LIST_FIND, $3612): for each, BREAK tested (NextZXOS ROM 1's BREAK_STOP), the line copied\nto $5CB6 (ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY), its number and text expanded (LINE_START_NUM,\nEXPAND_NEXT) and printed, a 0 as a space. Ends at a line number from $2800 up (the program's\nend).\nExit: bank 7.","comment":"The line's address kept"},
        "6627": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6628": {"comment":"The expansion reset"},
        "6631": {"synopsis":"One line: BREAK, then a copy of it at $5CB6.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6632": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP"},
        "6635": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "6638": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "6640": {"comment":"ROM 1's BANK_LINE_COPY: HL = $5CB6"},
        "6643": {"comment":"Past the program's end?"},
        "6644": {"comment":"A number from $2800 up?"},
        "6646": {"comment":"DE = the line's address"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "6648": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6649": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6653": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "6656": {"comment":"The next line's address kept"},
        "6657": {"comment":"Past its header and text"},
        "6662": {"comment":"The next line kept"},
        "6663": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6664": {"comment":"HL = the copy + 1"},
        "6666": {"comment":"Its number as text first"},
        "6669": {"synopsis":"The next character; none left: the next line."},
        "6672": {"comment":"None left: the next line"},
        "6674": {"comment":"Bank 0 while printing"},
        "6675": {"comment":"0?"},
        "6678": {"comment":"A space"},
        "6680": {"synopsis":"Printed (RST $28); bank 7; the next."},
        "6681": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6682": {"comment":"The next"},
        "6684": {"synopsis":"Counts the characters the line at HL expands to (its number and text; LINE_START_NUM, then\nEXPAND_NEXT until none is left). From NextZXOS ROM 1's ALT_1A1C_STUB ($03FA).\nExit: HL = the count; bank 0.","comment":"The line's address kept"},
        "6685": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6689": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "6691": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6694": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "6698": {"comment":"The count, one short"},
        "6701": {"synopsis":"One character counted."},
        "6706": {"comment":"One more"},
        "6707": {"comment":"While characters come"},
        "6709": {"comment":"Bank 0"}
      }
    },
