        "4813": {"comment":"16?"},
        "4817": {"comment":"No: 8 x 8"},
        "4823": {"synopsis":"LAYER OVER n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER OVER, the word at its $0517): the\nlayer order, 0-7 (report B otherwise), into bits 4-2 of NextReg $15 (through $05DA and\nNextZXOS ROM 1's NEXTREG_15_MASK; the other bits kept).","comment":"A = the order (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4838": {"comment":"0-7 only"},
        "4840": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "4842": {"comment":"To bits 4-2"},
        "4844": {"comment":"D = the bits kept in NextReg $15"},
        "4846": {"comment":"NextReg $15 = its other bits OR these ($05DA)"},
        "4849": {"synopsis":"LAYER AT x, y (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER AT, the word at its $051F): the\nscroll offsets of the current mode, x 0-255, y 0-191 (report B otherwise): NextRegs $32/$33\nfor LoRes, $16/$17 for Layer 2.","comment":"Checking: done; running: a mode that has tiles"},
        "4852": {"comment":"A = the second number, y (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4867": {"comment":"Below 192?"},
        "4869": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "4871": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4872": {"comment":"A = the first number, x (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4887": {"comment":"D = y"},
        "4888": {"comment":"E = x"},
        "4889": {"comment":"A = the mode (1 LoRes)"},
        "4892": {"comment":"L = NextReg $32: LoRes's X offset"},
        "4894": {"comment":"LoRes?"},
        "4895": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "4897": {"comment":"L = NextReg $16: Layer 2's X offset"},
        "4899": {"synopsis":"NextReg L = E, NextReg L + 1 = D (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXTREG_PAIR), then return.","comment":"NextReg L = E, L + 1 = D (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXTREG_PAIR)"},
        "4915": {"synopsis":"LAYER BANK n, m (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER BANK, the word at its $051B):\nLayer 2's RAM banks: n into NextReg $12 (the bank shown), m into NextReg $13 (the shadow\nbank). Each must be 9 or more (report B otherwise) and it and the two banks after it are\nchecked through NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3 ($330F).","comment":"A = the second bank (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4930": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4931": {"comment":"A = the first bank (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "4946": {"comment":"D = the second bank"},
        "4947": {"comment":"E = the first"},
        "4948": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4949": {"comment":"Banks 0-8 are not allowed"},
        "4954": {"comment":"Is the first one 9 or more?"},
        "4955": {"synopsis":"No carry: report B (ERR_B_2).","comment":"No: report B"},
        "4958": {"comment":"Three banks each (48K)"},
        "4960": {"synopsis":"Banks D and E checked.","comment":"Is bank D a bank? (NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3)"},
        "4976": {"comment":"The same bank twice?"},
        "4978": {"comment":"Yes: once is enough"},
        "4980": {"comment":"Is bank E a bank?"},
        "4995": {"synopsis":"The next bank of each.","comment":"The next bank of each"},
        "4997": {"comment":"Three times"},
        "4999": {"comment":"E = the first, D = the second"},
        "5000": {"comment":"NextReg $12 = E, $13 = D: Layer 2's banks"},
        "5002": {"comment":"Set them"},
        "5004": {"synopsis":"LAYER DIM a, b, c, d (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER DIM, the word at its\n$052E): the clip window of the current mode: NextReg $18 (Layer 2) or $1A (the ULA and\nLoRes), written a, b, c, d through NextZXOS ROM 1's CLIP_SET (entered at $152D, past its\nzeros). b and d must be below 192 (report B otherwise).","comment":"A Layer 2 mode ($5C7F bit 1)?"},
        "5008": {"comment":"L = NextReg $18: Layer 2's clip window"},
        "5010": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5012": {"comment":"L = NextReg $1A: the ULA's (and LoRes's) clip window"},
        "5014": {"synopsis":"The NextReg kept; the four numbers.","comment":"Kept"},
        "5015": {"comment":"A = the fourth number (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5030": {"comment":"Below 192?"},
        "5032": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "5035": {"comment":"E = the fourth"},
        "5036": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5037": {"comment":"A = the third number (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5052": {"comment":"D back"},
        "5053": {"comment":"D = the third"},
        "5054": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5055": {"comment":"A = the second number (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5070": {"comment":"Below 192?"},
        "5072": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "5075": {"comment":"C = the second"},
        "5076": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5077": {"comment":"A = the first number (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5092": {"comment":"C back"},
        "5093": {"comment":"B = the first"},
        "5094": {"comment":"D, E = the third, the fourth"},
        "5095": {"comment":"L = the clip window's NextReg"},
        "5096": {"comment":"Written as B, C, D, E (NextZXOS ROM 1's CLIP_SET past its zeros)"},
        "5112": {"synopsis":"LAYER ERASE x, y, w, h [, c] (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER ERASE, the word\nat its $0525; the optional colour is read here): fills a w x h block of the current mode's\nscreen at x, y with colour c, or with the global transparent colour (NextReg $14) without\none. w 1-256 (report B otherwise); $2CD2 checks the block fits (report B) and pages the\nscreen in; $2D51 gives each next row; on the other stack ($5B6A).","comment":"A colour after a ','?"},
        "5114": {"comment":"No"},
        "5116": {"comment":"Past ',', then a number (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6)"},
        "5131": {"comment":"Checking: done; running: a mode that has tiles"},
        "5134": {"comment":"A = the colour (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5149": {"comment":"Use it"},
        "5151": {"synopsis":"No colour: the global transparent one.","comment":"Checking: done; running: a mode that has tiles"},
        "5154": {"comment":"A = the global transparent colour (NextReg $14)"},
        "5157": {"synopsis":"$5B8A = the colour; the block's numbers.","comment":"$5B8A = the colour to fill with"},
        "5160": {"comment":"A = the fourth number, the height (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5175": {"comment":"D = the height"},
        "5176": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5177": {"comment":"BC = the third number, the width (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "5192": {"comment":"0?"},
        "5194": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "5196": {"comment":"Over 256?"},
        "5199": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "5201": {"comment":"D = the height"},
        "5202": {"comment":"E = the width less 1"},
        "5203": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5204": {"comment":"A = the second number, y (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5219": {"comment":"D = y"},
        "5220": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5221": {"comment":"A = the first number, x (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5236": {"comment":"D = y"},
        "5237": {"comment":"E = x"},
        "5238": {"comment":"B = the height, C = the width less 1"},
        "5239": {"comment":"Onto the other stack ($5B6A)"},
        "5242": {"comment":"H = the rows"},
        "5243": {"comment":"L = the width (0 for 256)"},
        "5245": {"comment":"DE = the screen address of x, y, paged in ($2CD2)"},
        "5248": {"synopsis":"One row.","comment":"The counts and address kept"},
        "5250": {"comment":"A = the colour"},
        "5253": {"synopsis":"One byte of it.","comment":"One byte"},
        "5254": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5255": {"comment":"One byte less in the row"},
        "5256": {"comment":"More?"},
        "5258": {"comment":"HL = the row's address"},
        "5259": {"comment":"DE = the next row's ($2D51)"},
        "5262": {"comment":"The counts"},
        "5263": {"comment":"One row less"},
        "5264": {"comment":"More rows?"},
        "5266": {"comment":"The screen's paging put back ($2D6E)"},
        "5269": {"synopsis":"Back from the other stack ($00EC), then return. TILE_DRAW ends here too.","comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "5273": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A, report B (NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A), as ERR_B.","comment":"Error code $0A: report B (NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A)"},
        "5290": {"synopsis":"PALETTE FORMAT n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE FORMAT, the word at its\n$0508): the ULANext ink mask n through NextZXOS ROM 1's SET_ULANEXT (0 turns ULANext off;\notherwise one less than a power of 2, report B otherwise).","comment":"A = the mask (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5305": {"comment":"The ULANext ink mask (NextZXOS ROM 1's SET_ULANEXT)"},
        "5321": {"synopsis":"SPRITE PALETTE n ... (jumped to from $0591, the SPRITE command's PALETTE): past PALETTE and\nits number, then PAL_LAYER_GO for the sprites' palettes ($28).","comment":"Past PALETTE, then a number (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6)"},
        "5336": {"comment":"$28: the sprites' palettes (NextReg $43 bits 6-4 = 010)"},
        "5338": {"comment":"On"},
        "5340": {"synopsis":"LAYER PALETTE n ... (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for LAYER PALETTE, the word at its\n$0514): the palettes of the current mode's layer ($14 for Layer 2, $02 for the ULA and\nLoRes), then PAL_LAYER_GO.","comment":"$14: Layer 2's palettes (bits 6-4 = 001)"},
        "5342": {"comment":"A Layer 2 mode ($5C7F bit 1)?"},
        "5346": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5348": {"comment":"$02: the ULA's palettes (bits 6-4 = 000)"},
        "5350": {"synopsis":"The palette commands, n (0 or 1, the first or second palette) on the calculator stack and\n$5B8A = the layer (bits 5-4 its value for NextReg $43 bits 5-4, bits 3-1 its active-palette\nbit there):\n1. n alone: palette n becomes the layer's active one (PAL_SELECT).\n2. n BANK b, o: palette n loaded from bank b at offset o (PAL_BANK_LOAD).\n3. n, i, v: entry i of palette n = the 9-bit colour v (0-511, report B otherwise), through\n   NextRegs $40 and $44.\n4. Anything else: report C ($06D7).","comment":"$5B8A = the layer: bits 5-4 select, bits 3-1 its active-palette bit"},
        "5353": {"comment":"A = the character after the number"},
        "5354": {"comment":"Z at ENTER or ':' (NextZXOS ROM 1's STMT_END_TEST)"},
        "5369": {"comment":"The statement's end: choose the active palette"},
        "5371": {"comment":"BANK?"},
        "5373": {"comment":"Yes: load a palette from a bank"},
        "5376": {"comment":"','?"},
        "5378": {"comment":"Anything else: report C"},
        "5381": {"comment":"Past ',', then two numbers (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "5396": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "5399": {"comment":"BC = the colour (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "5414": {"comment":"Over 511?"},
        "5417": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "5420": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5421": {"comment":"A = the entry (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5436": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5437": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5452": {"comment":"It chosen for writing"},
        "5455": {"comment":"A = the entry"},
        "5456": {"comment":"The palette's index"},
        "5459": {"comment":"DE = the colour"},
        "5460": {"comment":"E = bits 8-1, D bit 0 = bit 0"},
        "5466": {"comment":"The first byte, RRRGGGBB"},
        "5470": {"comment":"Then the last blue bit"},
        "5475": {"synopsis":"n alone: palette n (0 or 1, report B otherwise) becomes the layer's active one: its bit in\nNextReg $43 set or cleared (PAL_CTRL_MASK).","comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "5478": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5493": {"comment":"0 or 1 only"},
        "5495": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "5498": {"comment":"L = the palette"},
        "5499": {"comment":"D = the layer's active-palette bit"},
        "5505": {"comment":"E = every other bit"},
        "5507": {"comment":"The second palette?"},
        "5509": {"comment":"Yes: the bit set"},
        "5511": {"comment":"The first: the bit cleared"},
        "5513": {"synopsis":"NextReg $43 = (NextReg $43 AND E) OR D.","comment":"NextReg $43 changed"},
        "5516": {"synopsis":"n BANK b, o: palette n chosen for writing from entry 0; bank b paged at $C000 (checked\nthrough NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3, offset o below $4000) on the other stack; its 256\nentries from $C000 + o: one byte each (NextReg $41), or two each (NextReg $44 twice) when\nPALETTE DIM 9 set $5C7F bit 4. Running past the bank's end is report B (ERR_B_BANK0). RAM\nbank 0 and the normal stack back at the end ($00E8).","comment":"Past BANK, then two numbers (NextZXOS ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_8)"},
        "5531": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "5534": {"comment":"BC = the offset (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_WORD)"},
        "5549": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5550": {"comment":"A = the bank (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5565": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5566": {"comment":"A = the palette, 0 or 1 (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5581": {"comment":"It chosen for writing"},
        "5584": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "5588": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "5589": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "5590": {"comment":"Bank A, offset HL checked (NextZXOS ROM 1's BANK_PAGE_ROM3)"},
        "5605": {"comment":"Onto the other stack ($5B6A)"},
        "5608": {"comment":"The offset at $C000-$FFFF"},
        "5612": {"comment":"A = the bank's upper 8K page"},
        "5615": {"comment":"And the lower one, at $C000"},
        "5619": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "5620": {"comment":"BC = 255: the last byte of 256"},
        "5623": {"comment":"9-bit entries ($5C7F bit 4)?"},
        "5627": {"comment":"No"},
        "5629": {"comment":"511: the last of 512"},
        "5630": {"synopsis":"Does the palette run past $FFFF?","comment":"Past the bank's end?"},
        "5631": {"comment":"DE = the start"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "5635": {"comment":"256 entries"},
        "5637": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"A = the next byte"},
        "5639": {"comment":"9-bit entries?"},
        "5643": {"comment":"No"},
        "5645": {"comment":"The first byte, RRRGGGBB"},
        "5648": {"comment":"Then the second, its blue bit"},
        "5653": {"comment":"On"},
        "5655": {"synopsis":"An 8-bit entry.","comment":"One 8-bit entry"},
        "5658": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"One entry less"},
        "5659": {"comment":"More?"},
        "5661": {"comment":"RAM bank 0 and the normal stack back"},
        "5665": {"synopsis":"Chooses palette A (0 or 1, report B otherwise) of the layer in $5B8A for reading and\nwriting: NextReg $43 bit 6 = A, bits 5-4 = the layer's; bits 7 and 3-0 kept (PAL_CTRL_MASK).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"0 or 1 only"},
        "5667": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "5670": {"comment":"Bit 6: the palette"},
        "5673": {"comment":"Bits 5-4: the layer's"},
        "5680": {"comment":"E: bits 7 and 3-0 kept"},
        "5682": {"synopsis":"NextReg $43 = (NextReg $43 AND E) OR D: read through $0A9B (port $243B selected, port $253B\nread), written back through port $253B.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"A = NextReg $43, read through port $253B ($0A9B)"},
        "5687": {"comment":"Its kept bits"},
        "5688": {"comment":"With the new ones"},
        "5689": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "5692": {"synopsis":"PALETTE DIM n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE DIM, the word at its $0505): n\n8 or 9 (report B otherwise): the width of the entries PAL_BANK_LOAD reads, kept in $5C7F bit\n4 (set for 9).","comment":"A = 8 or 9 (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5707": {"comment":"8 or 9 less 8"},
        "5709": {"comment":"Below 8: report B"},
        "5712": {"comment":"0 or 1?"},
        "5714": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "5717": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 4 cleared: 8-bit entries"},
        "5721": {"comment":"8?"},
        "5722": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "5723": {"comment":"9: $5C7F bit 4 set"},
        "5728": {"synopsis":"PALETTE OVER n (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for PALETTE OVER, the word at its $050B):\nn becomes the transparent colour, the global one (NextReg $14) and the sprites' index\n(NextReg $4B), through NextZXOS ROM 1 at $15BE.","comment":"A = the colour (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "5743": {"comment":"The transparent colour in NextRegs $14 and $4B ($15BE)"},
        "5759": {"synopsis":"PLAY a$, b$, ... (from NextZXOS ROM 1's syntax entry for token $A4, the word at its $0392):\n1 to 9 strings (ROM 3's CLASS_A each; 10 or more is error code $0B, report C), then\nPLAY_RUN.","comment":"No strings yet"},
        "5761": {"synopsis":"One more string.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "5762": {"comment":"A string (ROM 3's CLASS_A)"},
        "5765": {"comment":"The count"},
        "5766": {"comment":"One more"},
        "5767": {"comment":"A ',' after it?"},
        "5769": {"comment":"No: the last"},
        "5771": {"comment":"Past the ','"},
        "5772": {"comment":"The next string"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"B = the strings: up to 9.","comment":"The count"},
        "5775": {"comment":"Up to 9"},
        "5777": {"comment":"Fine"},
        "5779": {"comment":"Too many: error code $0B, report C (NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A)"},
        "5796": {"synopsis":"Plays the B strings on the calculator stack together on the three AY chips (TurboSound),\ninterrupts off; as the 128K ROM 0's PLAY_RUN, with these changes: up to 9 strings, strings\n0-2 on AY 1, 3-5 on AY 2, 6-8 on AY 3 (channels A-C of each), each chip selected through\nport $FFFD before its registers are written; the strings' ended bits and the current\nstring's bit are words at $5CAE and $5CAC; no MIDI is sent; three more commands, L, R and S\n(the chip's audio left, right or both).\n1. Checking syntax ends here. Room in the workspace for a 55-byte block per string and a\n   55-byte shared one (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM): IY at the shared one, IX at each string's from\n   the top down, filled with the defaults and the string's place and end (NextZXOS ROM 1's\n   STK_FETCH, the last string first); each block's address into the shared list.\n2. PLAY_SETUP: the tempo's delay, TEMPO_CODE copied, every chip's mixer and envelope period\n   set (AY_WRITE_ALL), the chip-select bytes at $5CA6-$5CA8 = $FF, $FE, $FD (AY 1-3, both\n   audio sides on).\n3. Each string's first note read (PLAY_NEXT); then until every string has ended: the\n   shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST), the notes started (PLAY_START_NOTES), that long waited\n   (PLAY_WAIT), the lengths moved on (PLAY_ADVANCE).\n4. At the end the AY chips silenced (PLAY_SILENCE) and interrupts on.\nA string's block (IX, 55 bytes) is the 128K's: +0 the note sounding, +1 its MIDI channel\n($FF none), +2 its number (0-8), +3 the octave's base note, +4 the volume (bit 4: the\nenvelope), +5 the length, +6 the place in the string, +8 its end, +10 flags, +11 the bracket\ndepth and +12 the brackets' places, +22 the repeat depth and +23 its places, +33 the lengths\nleft, +34 the lengths.\nThe shared block (IY, 55 bytes): +0 the blocks' addresses, +18 each string's pointer to its\ncurrent length, +36 the place in one of the lists, +38 the shortest length, +40 the tempo's\ndelay, +42 TEMPO_CODE's copy.","comment":"Checking syntax: the statement ends here"},
        "5799": {"comment":"C = the strings"},
        "5800": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5801": {"comment":"HL = 55 x (strings + 1): a block each and a shared one"},
        "5807": {"synopsis":"55 bytes for each string.","comment":"55 more"},
        "5810": {"comment":"BC = the room"},
        "5812": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "5815": {"comment":"No interrupts"},
        "5816": {"comment":"IY = the shared block, at the room's start"},
        "5819": {"comment":"IX = the room's end + 1"},
        "5823": {"comment":"$5CAE = $FFFF: every string ended for now"},
        "5829": {"synopsis":"The next string's block, from the top down: the octave 60, no MIDI channel, volume 15,\nlength 5, nothing tied, no brackets or repeats; its place and end (NextZXOS ROM 1's\nSTK_FETCH); its address into the shared list; its bit in $5CAE cleared (a 0 shifted in).","comment":"IX back 55 bytes: the next string's block, from the top down"},
        "5834": {"comment":"B = the strings left"},
        "5836": {"comment":"Volume 15"},
        "5838": {"comment":"The octave's base: note 60"},
        "5842": {"comment":"No MIDI channel"},
        "5846": {"comment":"The volume"},
        "5849": {"comment":"The length: 5"},
        "5853": {"comment":"Nothing tied"},
        "5857": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "5861": {"comment":"No brackets"},
        "5865": {"comment":"No repeat"},
        "5869": {"comment":"The repeat's places"},
        "5877": {"comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length (NextZXOS ROM 1's STK_FETCH)"},
        "5892": {"comment":"Its place"},
        "5898": {"comment":"The place to go back to when no '(' is open"},
        "5904": {"comment":"HL = the string's end"},
        "5906": {"comment":"Kept at IX + 8"},
        "5912": {"comment":"B = the strings left"},
        "5914": {"comment":"The string's number, from 0"},
        "5918": {"comment":"X 2"},
        "5920": {"comment":"HL = IY + 2 x the number: its entry in the list"},
        "5924": {"comment":"BC = the block's address"},
        "5927": {"comment":"Into the list"},
        "5930": {"comment":"$5CAE shifted left: the string not ended"},
        "5937": {"comment":"B = the strings left"},
        "5938": {"comment":"One less"},
        "5940": {"comment":"IX + 2 = the string's number"},
        "5943": {"comment":"More strings?"},
        "5945": {"synopsis":"The tempo's delay ($0B1A) at IY + 40, TEMPO_CODE copied to IY + 42; on every chip the mixer\n$F8 (tones on A-C, no noise) and the envelope period $FFFF; the chip-select bytes; then the\nplay loop.","comment":"BC = the count, off the stack"},
        "5946": {"comment":"IY + 40 = $0B1A: the tempo's delay at first"},
        "5954": {"comment":"DE = IY + 42"},
        "5962": {"comment":"TEMPO_CODE copied there"},
        "5970": {"comment":"Register 7, the mixer: tones on A-C, no noise"},
        "5974": {"comment":"On all three AY chips"},
        "5977": {"comment":"Registers 11 and 12, the envelope period: $FFFF"},
        "5988": {"comment":"The chip-select bytes for port $FFFD: AY 1"},
        "5994": {"comment":"AY 2"},
        "5997": {"comment":"AY 3, each with both audio sides on"},
        "5999": {"comment":"The list from its start; string 0's bit"},
        "6002": {"synopsis":"The next string: ended ones are passed by.","comment":"Has this string ended?"},
        "6005": {"comment":"Yes: the next"},
        "6007": {"comment":"IX = its block, its AY chip selected"},
        "6010": {"comment":"Its next note (PLAY_NEXT)"},
        "6013": {"synopsis":"The next string's bit; after the last, the notes.","comment":"The next string's bit; Z until past string 8"},
        "6016": {"comment":"More strings"},
        "6018": {"synopsis":"The shortest length (PLAY_SHORTEST), the notes started (PLAY_START_NOTES).","comment":"DE = the shortest length now"},
        "6021": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6022": {"comment":"Every string's note started"},
        "6025": {"comment":"DE = the shortest length"},
        "6026": {"synopsis":"Have all the strings ended? Then the AY chips silenced, interrupts on, done.","comment":"Have all the strings ended ($5CAE = $FFFF)?"},
        "6032": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6034": {"comment":"Yes: the AY silenced"},
        "6037": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "6039": {"synopsis":"The shortest length waited (PLAY_WAIT), the lengths moved on (PLAY_ADVANCE), the next\nshortest; again.","comment":"The units less 1"},
        "6040": {"comment":"Waited"},
        "6043": {"comment":"The lengths moved on, new notes read and started"},
        "6046": {"comment":"The next shortest length"},
        "6049": {"comment":"Again"},
        "6051": {"synopsis":"Copied into the shared block and run there with ROM 3 paged in (PLAY_TEMPO, through $00A7):\nRST $28 and calculator codes stk-ten, exchange, division, a literal, division, end-calc,\nthen RET: the tempo's delay from T's number. The 128K ROM 0's 13 bytes unchanged."},
        "6064": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK as the 128K's PLAY_BREAK does; with SPACE and CAPS SHIFT both down it is still\nno BREAK when NextZXOS ROM 1's TAPE_BREAK_TEST gives NZ (BREAK ignored).\nExit: carry unless BREAK.","comment":"Keyboard row SPACE-B"},
        "6066": {"comment":"SPACE (bit 0) not down?"},
        "6069": {"comment":"Not down: carry, no BREAK"},
        "6070": {"comment":"Keyboard row CAPS SHIFT-V"},
        "6072": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT (bit 0) not down?"},
        "6075": {"comment":"Not down: carry, no BREAK"},
        "6076": {"comment":"Both down: is BREAK ignored? (NextZXOS ROM 1's TAPE_BREAK_TEST)"},
        "6091": {"comment":"Ignored: carry"},
        "6093": {"comment":"BREAK: no carry"},
        "6095": {"synopsis":"The list of length pointers (IY + 18); then PLAY_LIST_SET.","comment":"BC = 18: the list of length pointers (IY + 18)"},
        "6098": {"comment":"On"},
        "6100": {"synopsis":"The list of blocks from its start (IY + 0); then PLAY_LIST_SET.","comment":"BC = 0: the list of blocks (IY + 0)"},
        "6103": {"synopsis":"$5CAC = 1, string 0's bit; IY + 36 = HL = IY + BC, the place in the list.","comment":"$5CAC = 1: string 0's bit"},
        "6109": {"comment":"HL = IY + BC"},
        "6113": {"comment":"IY + 36 = the list's place"},
        "6120": {"synopsis":"IX = the block whose address is at HL; then PLAY_AY_SELECT.","comment":"DE = the block's address from the list"},
        "6123": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "6126": {"synopsis":"Selects the AY chip of the string at IX: its chip-select byte ($5CA6 for strings 0-2, $5CA7\nfor 3-5, $5CA8 for 6-8) sent to port $FFFD.\nExit: A = the byte, HL = its address, BC = $FFFD.","comment":"A = the string's number"},
        "6129": {"comment":"HL = AY 1's chip-select byte, for strings 0-2"},
        "6132": {"comment":"0-2?"},
        "6136": {"comment":"AY 2's, for strings 3-5"},
        "6137": {"comment":"3-5?"},
        "6141": {"comment":"AY 3's, for strings 6-8"},
        "6142": {"synopsis":"The byte sent.","comment":"A = the chip-select byte"},
        "6143": {"comment":"The TurboSound control port"},
        "6146": {"comment":"The string's chip selected"},
        "6149": {"synopsis":"HL = the envelope shape kept for the string's chip: $5CA9 for strings 0-2, $5CAA for 3-5,\n$5CAB for 6-8.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the string's number"},
        "6152": {"comment":"HL = AY 1's envelope shape ($5CA9), for strings 0-2"},
        "6155": {"comment":"0-2?"},
        "6158": {"comment":"AY 2's ($5CAA)"},
        "6159": {"comment":"3-5?"},
        "6162": {"comment":"AY 3's ($5CAB)"},
        "6164": {"synopsis":"A = the string's AY channel on its chip: its number (IX + 2) less 3 or 6, 0-2.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"A = the string's number"},
        "6167": {"comment":"0-2?"},
        "6169": {"comment":"As it is"},
        "6170": {"comment":"Less 3"},
        "6172": {"comment":"Was it 3-5?"},
        "6175": {"comment":"6-8: less 6"},
        "6178": {"synopsis":"NZ when the current string has ended: $5CAE AND $5CAC is not 0. The main registers are kept\n(EXX).","comment":"The other registers kept"},
        "6179": {"comment":"HL = the ended bits"},
        "6182": {"comment":"DE = the current string's bit"},
        "6186": {"comment":"H AND D"},
        "6189": {"comment":"OR (L AND E): NZ when the string has ended"},
        "6192": {"comment":"The registers back"},
        "6194": {"synopsis":"The next string: $5CAC shifted left, then PLAY_LIST_NEXT.\nExit: Z while it is string 0-8 (bit 9 clear).","comment":"HL = the current string's bit"},
        "6197": {"comment":"The next string's"},
        "6198": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6201": {"comment":"Z while it is string 0-8 (bit 9 clear)"},
        "6203": {"synopsis":"The list's place (IY + 36) moved on to the next entry.\nExit: HL = it; the flags kept.","comment":"HL = the list's place"},
        "6209": {"comment":"2 bytes on"},
        "6211": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6218": {"synopsis":"PLAY's command letters, searched by PLAY_FIND_LETTER (CPIR from here): S R L H Z Y X W U V M\nT ) ( N O !. The 128K's 14 with S, R and L added in front."},
        "6235": {"synopsis":"The string's next character, past spaces and ENTERs (PLAY_SKIP_SPACE).\nExit: carry at the string's end; otherwise A and the place moved on.","comment":"The next character, past spaces and ENTERs"},
        "6238": {"comment":"The string's end: carry"},
        "6239": {"comment":"The place on by 1"},
        "6247": {"synopsis":"A note's name: '#' sharp (+1), '$' flat (-1), any number of each; a capital A-G an octave\nhigher than the small letter; the note from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE.\nExit: A = the note within its octave, or $80 for '&' (a rest); at the string's end it is\nmarked as ended. Anything else is report k.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "6248": {"comment":"C = the sharps less the flats, so far"},
        "6250": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6253": {"comment":"The string's end"},
        "6255": {"comment":"'&', a rest?"},
        "6257": {"comment":"No"},
        "6259": {"comment":"A = $80: a rest"},
        "6261": {"synopsis":"Done.","comment":"HL back"},
        "6263": {"synopsis":"The string's end: its bit set in $5CAE.","comment":"Marked as ended"},
        "6266": {"comment":"Done"},
        "6268": {"synopsis":"'#': one higher.","comment":"'#'?"},
        "6270": {"comment":"No"},
        "6272": {"comment":"One higher"},
        "6273": {"comment":"Next"},
        "6275": {"synopsis":"'$': one lower.","comment":"'$'?"},
        "6277": {"comment":"No"},
        "6279": {"comment":"One lower"},
        "6280": {"comment":"Next"},
        "6282": {"synopsis":"A small letter (bit 5 set) as it is; a capital 12 higher.","comment":"A small letter?"},
        "6284": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "6286": {"comment":"A capital: an octave (12) higher"},
        "6292": {"synopsis":"A-G only (report k otherwise): its place in the octave from PLAY_NOTE_TABLE, plus the sharps\nand flats.","comment":"A-G as 0-6 (either case)"},
        "6296": {"comment":"Below A: report k"},
        "6299": {"comment":"Past G?"},
        "6301": {"comment":"Yes: report k"},
        "6304": {"comment":"The sharps and flats kept"},
        "6305": {"comment":"BC = the letter"},
        "6308": {"comment":"HL = its entry in PLAY_NOTE_TABLE"},
        "6312": {"comment":"A = its note in the octave"},
        "6313": {"comment":"C = the sharps and flats"},
        "6314": {"comment":"Added"},
        "6315": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6317": {"synopsis":"Reads the decimal number at the string's place (none is 0), moving past it.\nExit: BC = the number; over 65535 is report l.","comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "6319": {"comment":"HL = the string's place"},
        "6325": {"comment":"DE = 0: the number so far"},
        "6328": {"synopsis":"The next digit.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "6329": {"comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "6331": {"comment":"Yes: the number's end"},
        "6333": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "6335": {"comment":"Yes: the number's end"},
        "6337": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6338": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6339": {"comment":"DE = DE x 10"},
        "6342": {"comment":"The digit"},
        "6344": {"comment":"HL = the digit"},
        "6347": {"comment":"Plus DE x 10"},
        "6348": {"comment":"Over 65535: report l"},
        "6350": {"comment":"DE = the number so far"},
        "6351": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "6352": {"comment":"The next digit"},
        "6354": {"synopsis":"Report l.","comment":"Report l"},
        "6357": {"synopsis":"The place stored; BC = the number.","comment":"The place kept"},
        "6363": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6365": {"comment":"DE and HL back"},
        "6368": {"synopsis":"DE = DE x 10; a carry is report l.","comment":"HL = 0"},
        "6371": {"comment":"Ten times"},
        "6373": {"synopsis":"Ten additions.","comment":"DE added"},
        "6374": {"comment":"Over 65535: report l"},
        "6376": {"comment":"Again"},
        "6378": {"comment":"DE = DE x 10"},
        "6380": {"synopsis":"Reads the current string up to its next note: BREAK stops it all (error code $14, report L,\nafter PLAY_SILENCE); each character: a command letter runs its routine from PLAY_COMMANDS;\nanything else is a note (PLAY_NOTE), which returns past PLAY_NEXT's loop. The string's end\nmarks it ended.","comment":"BREAK?"},
        "6383": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6385": {"comment":"Yes: the AY silenced"},
        "6388": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "6389": {"comment":"And error code $14, report L (NextZXOS ROM 1's ERROR_128_A)"},
        "6406": {"synopsis":"A character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6409": {"comment":"The string's end: marked as ended"},
        "6412": {"comment":"Is it a command letter? C = its index, 0 for none"},
        "6415": {"comment":"BC = 2 x the index"},
        "6419": {"comment":"HL = its entry in PLAY_COMMANDS"},
        "6423": {"comment":"DE = the routine"},
        "6426": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "6427": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "6430": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6432": {"comment":"Never reached"},
        "6433": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL.","comment":"To the command's routine"},
        "6434": {"synopsis":"'!': everything to the next '!' (or the end) is skipped.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6437": {"comment":"The string's end: marked as ended, PLAY_NEXT left"},
        "6440": {"comment":"'!'?"},
        "6442": {"comment":"Yes: the comment's end"},
        "6443": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6445": {"synopsis":"O n: the octave, 0-8 (report n otherwise): the base note 12 x n.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6448": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6449": {"comment":"0-8 only"},
        "6451": {"comment":"Otherwise report n"},
        "6454": {"comment":"X 4"},
        "6459": {"comment":"X 8"},
        "6461": {"comment":"Plus x 4: 12 x the octave"},
        "6462": {"comment":"The base note"},
        "6466": {"synopsis":"N: a separator; nothing to do.","comment":"N: nothing to do"},
        "6467": {"synopsis":"'(': one bracket deeper (report d at 5): its place kept, from IX + 12.","comment":"A = the bracket depth + 1"},
        "6471": {"comment":"A sixth?"},
        "6473": {"comment":"Report d"},
        "6476": {"comment":"The depth kept"},
        "6479": {"comment":"The list of '(' places, IX + 12"},
        "6482": {"comment":"HL = its entry"},
        "6485": {"comment":"The place, just past the '(', kept there"},
        "6495": {"synopsis":"')': the repeat. The first time at a ')' its place is kept and the string goes back to its\n'(' (or the start); the second time it goes on, the bracket closed. With no '(' left open,\nthe repeat goes on for ever.","comment":"A = the repeat depth"},
        "6498": {"comment":"The list of ')' places, IX + 23"},
        "6501": {"comment":"None yet?"},
        "6502": {"comment":"No ')' known yet: a new one"},
        "6505": {"comment":"HL = the last ')' kept"},
        "6508": {"comment":"The same ')' as now?"},
        "6512": {"comment":"No: a new one"},
        "6519": {"comment":"No: a new one"},
        "6521": {"comment":"Yes: the second time here, the repeat done"},
        "6524": {"comment":"A = the repeat depth"},
        "6528": {"comment":"Some left: on, past the ')'"},
        "6529": {"comment":"No '(' left open (IX + 10 bit 0)?"},
        "6533": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6534": {"comment":"Yes: the repeat again, for ever"},
        "6538": {"comment":"A = 0: back to the start for ever"},
        "6539": {"comment":"Go back"},
        "6541": {"synopsis":"A new ')': kept (report d at 5), then back to the '('.","comment":"A = the repeat depth + 1"},
        "6545": {"comment":"A sixth?"},
        "6547": {"comment":"Report d"},
        "6550": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6553": {"comment":"HL = its entry"},
        "6556": {"comment":"This ')' kept, the place"},
        "6565": {"comment":"A = the bracket depth"},
        "6568": {"synopsis":"The place back to bracket A's; one bracket less.","comment":"The list of '(' places"},
        "6571": {"comment":"HL = this one's entry"},
        "6574": {"comment":"The place back there"},
        "6583": {"comment":"One bracket less"},
        "6586": {"comment":"Some left: done"},
        "6587": {"comment":"None open: depth 0"},
        "6591": {"comment":"And IX + 10 bit 0: the start is the '('"},
        "6596": {"synopsis":"HL = IX + DE + 2 x A: an entry of one of the block's lists.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "6599": {"comment":"+ DE"},
        "6600": {"comment":"+ 2 x A"},
        "6607": {"synopsis":"T n: the tempo, 60-240 (report n otherwise), set only by string 0: 4 x n stacked (NextZXOS\nROM 1's STACK_BC) and TEMPO_CODE run in the shared block with ROM 3 paged in ($00A7); its\nresult (NextZXOS ROM 1's FP_TO_BC) is the delay at IY + 40.","comment":"BC = the tempo"},
        "6610": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "6612": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "6615": {"comment":"Below 60?"},
        "6618": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "6621": {"comment":"Over 240?"},
        "6623": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "6626": {"comment":"String 0?"},
        "6630": {"comment":"No: only string 0 sets the tempo"},
        "6631": {"comment":"BC = 4 x the tempo"},
        "6639": {"comment":"IX and IY kept"},
        "6643": {"comment":"IY = $5C3A for ROM 3's calculator"},
        "6647": {"comment":"4 x the tempo stacked (NextZXOS ROM 1's STACK_BC)"},
        "6662": {"comment":"HL = the shared block"},
        "6664": {"comment":"Plus 42: TEMPO_CODE's copy"},
        "6668": {"comment":"BC = its address"},
        "6670": {"comment":"Run with ROM 3 paged in ($00A7)"},
        "6673": {"comment":"BC = the delay (NextZXOS ROM 1's FP_TO_BC)"},
        "6688": {"comment":"No interrupts"},
        "6689": {"comment":"IY and IX back"},
        "6693": {"comment":"IY + 40 = the tempo's delay"},
        "6700": {"synopsis":"M n: the mixer (AY register 7 of the string's chip) = NOT n, n 0-63 (report n otherwise).","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6703": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6704": {"comment":"0-63 only"},
        "6706": {"comment":"Otherwise report n"},
        "6709": {"comment":"Inverted: a set bit turns a channel off"},
        "6710": {"comment":"E = the mixer"},
        "6711": {"comment":"AY register 7, on the string's chip"},
        "6717": {"synopsis":"V n: the volume, 0-15 (report n otherwise), into the block and the string's AY volume\nregister (8 + its channel).","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6720": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6721": {"comment":"0-15 only"},
        "6723": {"comment":"Otherwise report n"},
        "6726": {"comment":"The volume kept"},
        "6729": {"comment":"A = the AY channel, 0-2"},
        "6732": {"comment":"Register 8 + the channel: its volume"},
        "6735": {"comment":"E = the volume"},
        "6736": {"comment":"Written"},
        "6740": {"synopsis":"U: the volume $1F, the envelope's (bit 4).","comment":"The envelope's volume ($1F: bit 4)"},
        "6742": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6746": {"synopsis":"W n: the envelope shape, 0-7 (report n otherwise), through PLAY_SHAPES, kept for the\nstring's chip (PLAY_SHAPE_ADDR).","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6749": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6750": {"comment":"0-7 only"},
        "6752": {"comment":"Otherwise report n"},
        "6755": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "6757": {"comment":"HL = its entry in PLAY_SHAPES"},
        "6761": {"comment":"C = the AY envelope shape"},
        "6762": {"comment":"HL = the chip's shape byte"},
        "6765": {"comment":"Kept there"},
        "6767": {"synopsis":"X n: the envelope period (AY registers 11 and 12 of the string's chip) = n.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6770": {"comment":"Register 11 = its low byte"},
        "6776": {"comment":"Register 12 = its high byte"},
        "6782": {"synopsis":"Y n: the MIDI channel, 1-16 (report n otherwise), kept as n - 1; nothing here sends MIDI.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6785": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6786": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "6787": {"comment":"0 was: report n"},
        "6790": {"comment":"1-16 only"},
        "6792": {"comment":"Otherwise report n"},
        "6795": {"comment":"The MIDI channel kept, 0-15"},
        "6799": {"synopsis":"Z n: the number is read and ignored (the 128K sends it to MIDI).","comment":"The number read and ignored: no MIDI is sent"},
        "6803": {"synopsis":"H: all the strings ended at once ($5CAE = $FFFF).","comment":"$5CAE = $FFFF: every string ended"},
        "6810": {"synopsis":"L: the string's chip heard on the left only: bits 6-5 of its chip-select byte = 10, kept and\nsent to port $FFFD.","comment":"A = the chip-select byte, HL at it, BC = $FFFD"},
        "6813": {"comment":"Bits 6-5 = 10: left side only"},
        "6817": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6818": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6821": {"synopsis":"R: the string's chip heard on the right only: bits 6-5 of its chip-select byte = 01.","comment":"A = the chip-select byte, HL at it, BC = $FFFD"},
        "6824": {"comment":"Bits 6-5 = 01: right side only"},
        "6828": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6829": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6832": {"synopsis":"S: the string's chip heard on both sides: bits 6-5 of its chip-select byte = 11.","comment":"A = the chip-select byte, HL at it, BC = $FFFD"},
        "6835": {"comment":"Bits 6-5 = 11: both sides"},
        "6837": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6838": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6841": {"synopsis":"A note, with its length before it: no digit, the current length; 1-9 a length (it becomes\nthe current one), 10-12 a triplet (three notes of the length); '_' ties more lengths to it.\nThe lengths go into the block's list, the count at IX + 33; then PLAY_NEXT returns. A length\nof 0 or over 12 is report n; more than 10 lengths report o.","comment":"A digit?"},
        "6844": {"comment":"No: the current length, once"},
        "6847": {"comment":"HL = the block's length list"},
        "6850": {"comment":"The string's pointer to it = HL"},
        "6853": {"comment":"No lengths yet"},
        "6857": {"comment":"Back to the digit"},
        "6860": {"comment":"BC = the length's number"},
        "6863": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6864": {"comment":"0?"},
        "6865": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "6868": {"comment":"Over 12?"},
        "6870": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "6873": {"comment":"1-9?"},
        "6875": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6877": {"comment":"10-12, a triplet: DE = its units"},
        "6880": {"comment":"One more length"},
        "6883": {"comment":"The first of three"},
        "6886": {"synopsis":"A triplet length: twice more in the list.","comment":"One more length"},
        "6889": {"comment":"The second"},
        "6896": {"synopsis":"1-9: the current length.","comment":"1-9: the current length"},
        "6899": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "6902": {"synopsis":"One more length counted (report o past 10).","comment":"One more length"},
        "6905": {"synopsis":"'_'? Then the next length is added to it.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6908": {"comment":"'_', a tie?"},
        "6910": {"comment":"No: store the length"},
        "6912": {"comment":"Past the '_'"},
        "6915": {"comment":"BC = the next length's number"},
        "6918": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6919": {"comment":"1-9?"},
        "6921": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6923": {"comment":"A triplet length tied"},
        "6925": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "6928": {"comment":"HL = the units so far"},
        "6929": {"comment":"Plus these"},
        "6930": {"comment":"BC = these units"},
        "6932": {"comment":"DE = the sum"},
        "6933": {"comment":"HL = the list's place"},
        "6934": {"comment":"The sum stored"},
        "6937": {"comment":"DE = the triplet's units"},
        "6939": {"comment":"Two more of them"},
        "6941": {"synopsis":"A tied length added.","comment":"1-9: the current length"},
        "6946": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "6949": {"comment":"HL = the units so far"},
        "6950": {"comment":"Plus these"},
        "6951": {"comment":"DE = the sum"},
        "6952": {"comment":"HL = the list's place"},
        "6953": {"comment":"Another tie?"},
        "6956": {"synopsis":"The length stored; PLAY_NEXT ends.","comment":"The length stored"},
        "6959": {"comment":"PLAY_NEXT ended"},
        "6961": {"synopsis":"One more length in the list: 11 is report o.","comment":"A = the lengths so far + 1"},
        "6965": {"comment":"An eleventh?"},
        "6967": {"comment":"Report o"},
        "6970": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6974": {"synopsis":"No length given: the current one, once.","comment":"Back to the note's name"},
        "6977": {"comment":"One length"},
        "6981": {"comment":"HL = the block's length list"},
        "6984": {"comment":"The string's pointer to it"},
        "6987": {"comment":"C = the current length"},
        "6991": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "6995": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "6998": {"synopsis":"Returns two bytes past the call's return: past PLAY_NEXT's JR, which ends it.","comment":"The return address"},
        "6999": {"comment":"Moved past PLAY_NEXT's JR"},
        "7003": {"synopsis":"The string's end: the return address dropped (PLAY_NEXT left), its bit set in $5CAE.","comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "7004": {"synopsis":"The current string's bit ($5CAC) set in $5CAE.","comment":"HL = the ended bits"},
        "7007": {"comment":"The current string's bit added"},
        "7017": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7021": {"synopsis":"HL = the block's list of lengths (IX + 34).","comment":"HL = IX + 34"},
        "7029": {"synopsis":"The string's pointer to its current length (in IY's list at +18) = HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7030": {"comment":"HL = IY + 18"},
        "7037": {"comment":"+ 2 x the string's number"},
        "7045": {"comment":"DE = the list"},
        "7046": {"comment":"The pointer stored"},
        "7049": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "7051": {"synopsis":"The routines of PLAY's commands, from the index PLAY_FIND_LETTER gives (0 for none): a note\n(PLAY_NOTE), '!', O, N, '(', ')', T, M, V, U, W, X, Y, Z, H, L, R, S."},
        "7087": {"synopsis":"W's envelope shapes for 0-7: 0, 4, 11, 13, 8, 12, 14, 10."},
        "7095": {"synopsis":"Looks A up in PLAY_LETTERS (CPIR, BC = 18).\nExit: Z when found; C = its index from the end ('!' is 1, S is 17), 0 when not found.","comment":"18: 17 letters and one"},
        "7098": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_LETTERS"},
        "7101": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "7104": {"synopsis":"The notes A-G within an octave from C: 9, 11, 0, 2, 4, 5, 7."},
        "7111": {"synopsis":"DE = length C's units, from PLAY_LENGTHS. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7112": {"comment":"BC = the length's number"},
        "7114": {"comment":"HL = its entry in PLAY_LENGTHS"},
        "7118": {"comment":"DE = its units"},
        "7121": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7123": {"synopsis":"The lengths' units for 0-12: $80, then 1-9: 6, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 72, 96; 10-12\n(triplets): 4, 8, 16."},
        "7136": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "7138": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "7139": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "7141": {"comment":"No carry for a digit only"},
        "7143": {"synopsis":"Sounds note A (within the octave) on the string's chip and channel: the octave's base added\n(128 or more is report m); channel A of each chip also sets the chip's noise period (AY\nregister 6) from it; the tone period from PLAY_PERIODS (notes below 21 take $0FBF) into\nregisters 2n and 2n + 1, and with the envelope in use, register 13 = the chip's shape. Kept\nat IX + 0.","comment":"C = the note in the octave"},
        "7144": {"comment":"Plus the octave's base"},
        "7148": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "7150": {"comment":"Report m"},
        "7153": {"comment":"C = the note"},
        "7154": {"comment":"A = the AY channel"},
        "7157": {"comment":"Channel A of its chip?"},
        "7158": {"comment":"No"},
        "7160": {"comment":"Channel A: the noise period from the note"},
        "7164": {"comment":"A quarter"},
        "7168": {"comment":"Register 6"},
        "7171": {"comment":"Written"},
        "7174": {"synopsis":"The note kept; the tone.","comment":"The note kept"},
        "7177": {"comment":"A = the string's number"},
        "7180": {"comment":"9 or more?"},
        "7182": {"comment":"Never: there is no other string"},
        "7183": {"comment":"HL = PLAY_PERIODS"},
