        "8561": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8564": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8567": {"comment":"Printed in K, M or G ($240B)"},
        "8570": {"comment":"\" free\" and ENTER"},
        "8576": {"synopsis":"Nothing matched: \"No files found\" ($2475) unless an earlier part of the catalogue was\nprinted (entry 0's size byte, $F70B, not 0); then CAT_FREE.","comment":"Did any part come before (entry 0's size byte not 0)?"},
        "8580": {"comment":"\"No files found\""},
        "8583": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8586": {"comment":"Only when nothing came before"},
        "8589": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8592": {"comment":"The free space"},
        "8594": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A of ROM 3's keyword table (ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN, 0 = RND) with FLAGS bit 0\nset first, so no space goes before it. Called with $25 (LINE), $3F (DATA) and $0A (CODE) by\nTAPE_CAT.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL (what PRINT_TOKEN changes).","comment":"FLAGS bit 0: no space before the keyword"},
        "8598": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"CAT ASN (CAT followed by the token ASN, from $1F82): past ASN; checking ends at the\nstatement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each drive letter A-P ROM 2's\nIDE_DOS_MAPPING ($00F7) with L = $80 + the letter (the 256-byte form, BC = $D827): a mapped\ndrive prints as the letter, \": \" and the description ROM 2 left at $D827 ($FF-ended, ROM 1's\nPRINT_MSG), then ENTER. An error from ROM 2 goes to $2046. Ends in bank 0.","comment":"Past ASN"},
        "8603": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8606": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8609": {"comment":"16 drive letters"},
        "8611": {"comment":"From 'A'"},
        "8613": {"synopsis":"One letter: L = 'A'-'P', B the letters left.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8614": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "8615": {"comment":"BC = the 256-byte buffer for the description"},
        "8618": {"comment":"L = $80 + the letter: the long form"},
        "8620": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAPPING"},
        "8623": {"comment":"An error: $2046"},
        "8626": {"comment":"Not mapped: the next letter"},
        "8628": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "8630": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8634": {"comment":"':'"},
        "8639": {"comment":"' '"},
        "8644": {"comment":"The description, $FF-ended"},
        "8647": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG, back at $21D6"},
        "8662": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8665": {"synopsis":"The next letter; after P, bank 0.","comment":"The letter back"},
        "8666": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "8667": {"comment":"The next letter"},
        "8668": {"comment":"For 16 letters"},
        "8670": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8674": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB (CAT followed by the token TAB, from $1F87): lists the cards' partitions. Past TAB;\nchecking ends at the statement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each of 16 units:\n1. ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY ($01B4, C = the unit): a unit that fails is skipped (CAT_TAB_FREE).\n2. In bank 0: ENTER, \"Unit \", its number, \": \"; 16 bytes copied from IX (left by\n   IDE_CAPACITY) into 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) by ROM 2's $05CC and\n   printed; \", \" and the capacity (PRINT_SECTORS_A, no padding), ENTER.\n3. Every partition entry from 0 (CAT_TAB_ENTRY); unused ones counted; then the count and \"\n   free partition entries\" (CAT_TAB_FREE).\nEnds in bank 0.","comment":"Past TAB"},
        "8675": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8678": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8681": {"comment":"16 units"},
        "8683": {"synopsis":"One unit: A = 16 - B, the unit number; the free-entry count 0 kept on the stack under it.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8684": {"comment":"A = 16 - B, the unit number"},
        "8687": {"comment":"The free-entry count, 0"},
        "8691": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8692": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "8693": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY: DEHL = its sectors"},
        "8696": {"comment":"No such unit: on to the next"},
        "8699": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8701": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8704": {"comment":"The capacity kept (DEHL)"},
        "8706": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8707": {"comment":"ENTER, \"Unit \""},
        "8713": {"comment":"The unit number"},
        "8714": {"comment":"HL = the unit"},
        "8717": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8719": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $221E"},
        "8734": {"comment":"\": \""},
        "8740": {"comment":"17 bytes of workspace"},
        "8743": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8746": {"comment":"HL = IX, as IDE_CAPACITY left it"},
        "8749": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "8750": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "8753": {"comment":"ROM 2's $05CC (the DivMMC memory's copy routine)"},
        "8756": {"comment":"A = $A0 (PRINT_TEXT_DE does not read it)"},
        "8758": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "8759": {"comment":"Its text printed, up to a byte with bit 7 set"},
        "8762": {"comment":"\", \""},
        "8768": {"comment":"DEHL = the capacity again"},
        "8770": {"comment":"No padding"},
        "8772": {"comment":"The capacity, with its unit letter"},
        "8775": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8780": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8783": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "8786": {"synopsis":"Entry BC of the unit's partition table read into $F752 (ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, $00C4, A\n= the unit); an error goes to CAT_TAB_ERROR. Type 0 (the byte at $F762) is counted as free.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "8788": {"comment":"The entry's buffer"},
        "8791": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, entry BC"},
        "8794": {"comment":"An error: CAT_TAB_ERROR"},
        "8797": {"comment":"The entry's type"},
        "8800": {"comment":"0: an unused entry?"},
        "8802": {"comment":"No: a partition"},
        "8804": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8805": {"comment":"The free-entry count"},
        "8806": {"comment":"One more"},
        "8808": {"comment":"The unit kept again"},
        "8809": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "8812": {"synopsis":"A partition: \"u>\" (the unit's number, '>'), its 16-character name from $F752 with $00 shown\nas '~'; a space, its size (the 32-bit word at $F769 + 1, in 512-byte sectors,\nPRINT_SECTORS), a space and its type's name from PART_TYPE_NAMES; ENTER.","comment":"The unit"},
        "8814": {"comment":"The entry number kept"},
        "8815": {"comment":"HL = the unit"},
        "8818": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8820": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8823": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $2286"},
        "8838": {"comment":"'>' after the unit"},
        "8843": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8846": {"comment":"The name"},
        "8849": {"comment":"16 characters"},
        "8851": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"One character"},
        "8853": {"comment":"$00?"},
        "8856": {"comment":"Shown as '~'"},
        "8858": {"synopsis":"Printed; E counts the 16.","comment":"Printed in bank 0"},
        "8861": {"comment":"The next of the 16"},
        "8864": {"comment":"The type"},
        "8867": {"comment":"Plus 3: its name's number in the table"},
        "8870": {"comment":"DEHL = the 32-bit word at $F769"},
        "8877": {"comment":"plus 1: the size in sectors"},
        "8883": {"synopsis":"The size and the spaces round it, in bank 0; C = the type + 3, the type name's number in\nPART_TYPE_NAMES.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8886": {"comment":"The name's number kept"},
        "8887": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8892": {"comment":"The size, blanks before it"},
        "8895": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8900": {"comment":"C back"},
        "8901": {"comment":"The table of type names"},
        "8904": {"comment":"20 names at most"},
        "8906": {"synopsis":"Names skipped until C reaches 1 (20 at most).","comment":"Down to this name?"},
        "8909": {"synopsis":"One name's bytes, up to the one with bit 7 set.","comment":"The bytes of a name"},
        "8911": {"comment":"Bit 7 into the carry: the last?"},
        "8914": {"comment":"The next name"},
        "8916": {"synopsis":"The type's name printed (PRINT_TEXT_DE at $013D), ENTER; bank 7 again.","comment":"The type's name printed"},
        "8919": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8924": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8927": {"comment":"The entry number back"},
        "8928": {"synopsis":"The next entry, until BC wraps round to 0.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "8931": {"comment":"Until BC wraps round to 0"},
        "8934": {"synopsis":"The end of the unit's table: a free-entry count that is not 0 is printed with \" free\npartition entries\" and two ENTERs (MSG_FREE_ENTRIES).","comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8935": {"comment":"HL = the free-entry count"},
        "8936": {"comment":"None?"},
        "8940": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8942": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8945": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $2300"},
        "8960": {"comment":"\" free partition entries\", two ENTERs"},
        "8966": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8969": {"synopsis":"The next unit; after the 16th, bank 0.","comment":"The unit count back"},
        "8970": {"comment":"The next unit"},
        "8974": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8978": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ failed: error $38 is the table's end (CAT_TAB_FREE); $16 ends the unit\nwith no count; any other is reported ($2046).","comment":"Error $38: the end of the table"},
        "8980": {"comment":"Then the free-entry count"},
        "8982": {"comment":"Error $16: the unit has no table"},
        "8984": {"comment":"Others are reported"},
        "8987": {"comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8988": {"comment":"Drop the count"},
        "8989": {"comment":"The next unit, with no count"},
        "8991": {"synopsis":"CAT of the tape (from $1FF9, for a name of two characters starting 'T:'): lists the headers\non the tape until BREAK. 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) hold each header, IX at\nthem.\nThe same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT.","comment":"17 bytes for a header"},
        "8994": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8997": {"comment":"IX = the room"},
        "9000": {"synopsis":"A new line, then the next header (the same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9005": {"synopsis":"BREAK (SPACE, port $7FFE bit 0, and CAPS SHIFT, port $FEFE bit 0, both down) ends the list.","comment":"Port $7FFE: SPACE"},
        "9009": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "9010": {"comment":"SPACE not pressed: go on"},
        "9012": {"comment":"Port $FEFE: CAPS SHIFT"},
        "9016": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "9017": {"comment":"Not pressed: go on"},
        "9019": {"comment":"BREAK: done"},
        "9020": {"synopsis":"A header from the tape: flag 0, 17 bytes, loading (ROM 3's LD_BYTES); a failure tries again.\nThen the name in quotes and a space, and by the type: 0 \"BASIC \" and LINE n when it has a\nstart line; 1 and 2 TAPE_CAT_ARRAY; 3 TAPE_CAT_CODE; higher TAPE_CAT_LAYER.","comment":"The flag byte: a header"},
        "9022": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "9025": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "9026": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9028": {"comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "9031": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9033": {"comment":"Failed: try again"},
        "9035": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9037": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9042": {"comment":"10 characters of name"},
        "9044": {"synopsis":"One character of the name (header bytes 1-10).","comment":"One character"},
        "9050": {"comment":"On to the next"},
        "9052": {"comment":"For 10"},
        "9054": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9056": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9061": {"comment":"A space"},
        "9066": {"comment":"The type, header byte 0"},
        "9069": {"comment":"0, a program?"},
        "9071": {"comment":"No: other types"},
        "9073": {"comment":"\"BASIC \""},
        "9079": {"comment":"Header byte 14 bit 7: no start line?"},
        "9083": {"comment":"None: the next header"},
        "9085": {"comment":"LINE"},
        "9090": {"comment":"HL = the start line, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9096": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9098": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $2399"},
        "9113": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9115": {"synopsis":"Types 1 and 2, arrays: DATA, the array's letter (header byte 14, bit 7 off and bit 6 on),\nthen \"$() \" for type 2 or \"() \" for type 1 (MSG_ARRAY or one byte on).","comment":"Below 3: an array?"},
        "9117": {"comment":"No: CODE or higher"},
        "9119": {"comment":"The type kept"},
        "9120": {"comment":"DATA"},
        "9125": {"comment":"The array's name, header byte 14"},
        "9128": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "9130": {"comment":"Bit 6 on: a letter"},
        "9132": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9135": {"comment":"\"$() \""},
        "9138": {"comment":"The type back"},
        "9139": {"comment":"2, a string array?"},
        "9141": {"comment":"Yes: \"$() \""},
        "9143": {"comment":"No: \"() \""},
        "9144": {"synopsis":"The suffix printed.","comment":"Printed"},
        "9147": {"synopsis":"The next header (TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"The next header"},
        "9150": {"synopsis":"Type 3: CODE, the start (header bytes 13-14), ',' and the length (bytes 11-12).","comment":"Above 3: TAPE_CAT_LAYER"},
        "9152": {"comment":"CODE"},
        "9157": {"comment":"HL = the start, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9163": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9165": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $23DC"},
        "9180": {"comment":"','"},
        "9185": {"comment":"HL = the length, header bytes 11-12"},
        "9191": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9193": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $23F8"},
        "9208": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9210": {"synopsis":"Types 4 and up: ROM 1's SHOW_LAYER_KIND with A = the type; then the next header.","comment":"ROM 1's SHOW_LAYER_KIND, back at $2409"},
        "9225": {"comment":"The next header"},
        "9227": {"synopsis":"Prints a count of K: the size from ROM 2 in BCDE (K) doubled into DEHL, 512-byte sectors;\nthen PRINT_SECTORS. Called after DOS_FREE_SPACE (CAT_FREE_DRIVE) and by COPY_DATA with the K\ncopied so far.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = DE, the low word of BCDE"},
        "9228": {"comment":"Doubled: K into 512-byte sectors"},
        "9229": {"comment":"The carry into C and B"},
        "9233": {"comment":"DEHL = the sectors"},
        "9235": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL (in 512-byte sectors) with blanks before it (A = $20), as\nPRINT_SECTORS_A.","comment":"Blanks before the number"},
        "9237": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL, in 512-byte sectors, as a number and a unit letter: DE = 0 gives K\n(DEHL / 2), D = 0 M (DEHL / 2048), otherwise G (DEHL / 2^21), the quotient rounded up when\nbits are lost. The number goes through ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5 with E = A ($20 blanks before it,\n$FF none), the letter through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nEntry: A = the padding character for NUM_OUT_5.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The padding kept"},
        "9238": {"comment":"1 shift, 'K'"},
        "9241": {"comment":"DE = 0?"},
        "9243": {"comment":"Yes: K"},
        "9245": {"comment":"11 shifts, 'M'"},
        "9248": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "9250": {"comment":"Yes: M"},
        "9252": {"comment":"21 shifts, 'G'"},
        "9255": {"synopsis":"B = the shift count, C = the letter: the bits shifted out are ORed into A.","comment":"A collects the bits shifted out"},
        "9256": {"synopsis":"One shift of DEHL to the right.","comment":"DEHL one bit right"},
        "9264": {"comment":"The bit out into A"},
        "9266": {"comment":"B times"},
        "9268": {"comment":"Any bits lost?"},
        "9269": {"comment":"No"},
        "9271": {"comment":"Yes: rounded up"},
        "9272": {"synopsis":"E = the padding; the number printed, then the letter.","comment":"The padding back"},
        "9273": {"comment":"E = the padding for NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9274": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "9275": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $244A"},
        "9290": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "9291": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9296": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER (PRINT_A_BANK0).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9298": {"synopsis":"Prints A through ROM 3's PRINT_A with RAM bank 0 paged in ($00E8), then bank 7 again\n($00FF).\nChanges: AF (what PRINT_A changes).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9301": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9304": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9308": {"synopsis":"CAT's column move, bit 7 on its last byte: TAB ($17) to column 25 ($19, $00), then a space.\nPrinted by PRINT_TEXT_DE ($013D) from CAT_ENTRY_ATTRS."},
        "9312": {"synopsis":"\"BASIC \", bit 7 on the last byte (TAPE_CAT)."},
        "9318": {"synopsis":"\"$() \", bit 7 on the last byte; TAPE_CAT prints it for a string array and from $2467, \"() \",\nfor a number array."},
        "9322": {"synopsis":"\"<DIR>\", bit 7 on the last byte (CAT_NO_EXP)."},
        "9327": {"synopsis":"\" free\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_FREE_DRIVE)."},
        "9333": {"synopsis":"\"No files found\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_NO_FILES)."},
        "9348": {"synopsis":"ENTER and \"Unit \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9354": {"synopsis":"\": \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9356": {"synopsis":"\", \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9358": {"synopsis":"The partition types' names for CAT_TAB_TYPE, each ended by bit 7, number n for type n - 3:\n\"*BAD*\" ($FE), \"FREE\" ($FF), none (0), \"sys\" (1), \"swap\" (2), \"data\" (3), none (4-15, twelve\n$80s), \"FAT16\" ($10), \"FAT32\" ($11), none ($12)."},
        "9402": {"synopsis":"\" free partition entries\" and two ENTERs, bit 7 on the last (CAT_TAB_FREE)."},
        "9427": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO \"name\" (the syntax table's word at $048C, NextZXOS ROM 1, after classes $0A\nand $0C): ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS (checking ends there); the destination's name (on top of\nthe calculator stack) to $D827 in bank 7, $FF-ended (NAME_TO_HL); A = $10, a file, then\nCOPY_FILES.","comment":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS, back at $24E2"},
        "9442": {"comment":"The destination's name goes to $D827"},
        "9445": {"comment":"From the calculator stack, $FF-ended"},
        "9448": {"comment":"$10: the destination is a file"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Kept for COPY_FILES"},
        "9453": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO SCREEN$ or TO LPRINT (the syntax table's word at $048F): stream 3 when the\nsub-keyword kept at $5B5E is LPRINT ($E0), stream 2 otherwise; then COPY_STRM_SET.","comment":"The sub-keyword taken"},
        "9456": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "9458": {"comment":"Stream 3, the printer"},
        "9460": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9462": {"comment":"No: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "9463": {"synopsis":"A = the stream."},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO #n (the syntax table's word at $0493, after '#' and class 0): A = the stream\n(ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE); 16 or more is error code $0A (report B, ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"ROM 1's TAKE_BYTE, back at $2508"},
        "9480": {"comment":"Stream 0-15?"},
        "9482": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9484": {"comment":"Error code $0A (report B)"},
        "9486": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9501": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS (checking ends there); stream A made current (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).","comment":"The stream kept"},
        "9502": {"comment":"ROM 1's SCREEN_COLOURS, back at $252D"},
        "9517": {"comment":"The stream"},
        "9519": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "9522": {"synopsis":"Runs a COPY with the destination chosen (A on the stack: a stream 0-15, or $10 for a file\nnamed at $D827): the source's name to $E090 in bank 7, $FF-ended (NAME_TO_E090); bank 7;\n$D7FD = A. A file is COPY_TO_FILE. A stream lists the file: it is opened as file 0 (ROM 2's\nDOS_OPEN, $0106: B = 0, C = 1 read, D = 0, E = 1) and read a byte at a time (DOS_BYTE_READ,\n$0118); printable bytes and ENTER are printed in bank 0, BREAK tested after each (ROM 1's\nBREAK_STOP); other control codes are skipped, LF prints as ENTER unless it follows one, $1A\nor the file's end (error $19) closes it (DOS_CLOSE, $0109). Other errors go to DOS_FAIL.\nEnds in bank 0.","comment":"The source's name to $E090"},
        "9525": {"comment":"The stream, or $10 for a file"},
        "9526": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9529": {"comment":"Kept at $D7FD"},
        "9532": {"comment":"$10: a file?"},
        "9534": {"comment":"Yes: COPY_TO_FILE"},
        "9536": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9539": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9542": {"comment":"Open action 1, create action 0: it must exist"},
        "9545": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9548": {"comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9550": {"comment":"No byte before the first"},
        "9552": {"synopsis":"The next byte: D = the last one.","comment":"D = the last byte"},
        "9553": {"comment":"Kept over the call"},
        "9554": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9556": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_BYTE_READ: C = the byte"},
        "9559": {"comment":"D back"},
        "9560": {"comment":"A byte read?"},
        "9562": {"comment":"No: $19, the file's end?"},
        "9564": {"comment":"Another error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9567": {"comment":"The end: close it"},
        "9569": {"synopsis":"A byte read (C): $1A ends the file; ENTER is printed; LF goes to COPY_TYPE_LF; other codes\nbelow $20 are skipped.","comment":"The byte: $1A (soft EOF) also ends the file"},
        "9574": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "9576": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9578": {"comment":"LF?"},
        "9582": {"comment":"Another control code?"},
        "9584": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "9586": {"synopsis":"Printed in bank 0; BREAK tested (ROM 1's BREAK_STOP); bank 7.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9589": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9592": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP, back at $2587"},
        "9607": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9610": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "9612": {"synopsis":"The end: file 0 closed; bank 0.","comment":"File 0"},
        "9614": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9617": {"synopsis":"A failed open or close goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9619": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9623": {"synopsis":"LF: skipped after an ENTER, printed as ENTER otherwise.","comment":"ENTER: the byte before an ENTER?"},
        "9625": {"comment":"Then the LF is skipped"},
        "9628": {"comment":"Otherwise printed as ENTER"},
        "9630": {"synopsis":"COPY to a file: ENTER printed first. Also entered at COPY_TO_FILE_GO.","comment":"ENTER first"},
        "9635": {"synopsis":"COPY to a file, with the source's name at $E090 and the destination's at $D827 (bank 7,\n$FF-ended) and $D7FD set (bit 7: no messages, BREAK not tested). Also reached from NextZXOS\nROM 1's CALL_ALT_25A3 (the browser's copy, $D7FD = $80).\n1. $D5D6 = SP (DOS_FAIL comes back to it); $D7FE, the count of files copied, = 0.\n2. Both names parsed (PARSE_FILESPEC): the destination's results at $D822 (flags),\n   $D823-$D824 (user, drive) and $D825 (where its file name starts); the source's at $D81D,\n   $D81E-$D81F and $D820. A wildcard in the destination is error code $49.\n3. A wildcard in the source is COPY_WILD; a source with no file name is error code $2C.\n4. A destination with no file name is COPY_WILD too; otherwise COPY_ONE copies the file and\n   COPY_FILES_DONE reports.","comment":"SP kept for DOS_FAIL"},
        "9639": {"comment":"No files copied yet"},
        "9643": {"comment":"The destination's name"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "9649": {"comment":"Where its file name starts"},
        "9652": {"comment":"Its user area and drive"},
        "9656": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "9659": {"comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "9661": {"comment":"No"},
        "9663": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9666": {"comment":"Error code $49"},
        "9668": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9683": {"synopsis":"The source's name parsed.","comment":"The source's name"},
        "9686": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "9689": {"comment":"Where its file name starts"},
        "9692": {"comment":"Its user area and drive"},
        "9696": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "9699": {"comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "9701": {"comment":"Yes: COPY_WILD"},
        "9703": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name?"},
        "9705": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9707": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9710": {"comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "9712": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9727": {"synopsis":"Neither has a wildcard and the source has a name: a destination with a name is one file\n(COPY_ONE, COPY_FILES_DONE).","comment":"The destination's flags"},
        "9730": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name?"},
        "9732": {"comment":"No: COPY_WILD copies into the place"},
        "9734": {"comment":"One file copied"},
        "9737": {"comment":"Then the count"},
        "9740": {"synopsis":"A ROM 2 call failed, or COPY found an error, error code in A: files 2, 1 and 0 closed (ROM\n2's DOS_CLOSE, $0109), each one that will not close abandoned (DOS_ABANDON, $010C); ENTER.\nWith $D7FD bit 7 set (DOS_FAIL_QUIET) SP goes back to $D5D6's value and NC returns the error\nto COPY_TO_FILE_GO's caller; otherwise ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0 reports it.\nThe same job as the +3E's DOS_FAIL.","comment":"The error kept"},
        "9741": {"comment":"Files 2, 1 and 0"},
        "9743": {"synopsis":"One file: B = 2, 1, 0.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9744": {"comment":"B = the file"},
        "9746": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9749": {"comment":"B back"},
        "9750": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "9752": {"comment":"No: ROM 2's DOS_ABANDON"},
        "9755": {"synopsis":"The next file.","comment":"The count back"},
        "9756": {"comment":"The next file"},
        "9758": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "9763": {"comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9767": {"comment":"Yes: back to the caller"},
        "9769": {"comment":"The error"},
        "9770": {"comment":"ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0, which reports it"},
        "9785": {"synopsis":"Quiet: the error code back in A, the stack as COPY_TO_FILE_GO found it, NC.","comment":"The error back"},
        "9786": {"comment":"The stack as COPY_TO_FILE_GO found it"},
        "9790": {"comment":"NC: failed"},
        "9792": {"synopsis":"A wildcard in the source, or a destination with no file name: the destination must be a\ndrive, user area or path alone (error code $4A otherwise). Then each file that matches is\ncopied:\n1. The source's name copied to $DA31; the catalogue slot at $D810 cleared.\n2. COPY_CAT_NEXT: the last name found ($D810) preloaded at $D803 and the next matching file\n   asked for (ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG, $011E: B = 2, C = 2, LFN flags).\n3. Its long name (IDE_GET_LFN, $01B7, IX = the directory handle) written over the source's\n   file name ($D820 points into $E090).\n4. The destination's file name ($D825 on) made from it: the long name as it is when the\n   destination's drive has no XDPB (ROM 2's DOS_REF_XDPB, $0151, fails), otherwise the 8.3\n   name from the catalogue entry.\n5. BREAK tested unless $D7FD bit 7 is set; COPY_ONE; again.\nNo more matches: none copied is error $17; otherwise COPY_FILES_DONE.","comment":"The destination's flags"},
        "9795": {"comment":"A file name in the destination?"},
        "9797": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "9799": {"comment":"A drive, user area or path?"},
        "9801": {"comment":"Yes: go on"},
        "9803": {"synopsis":"Error code $4A (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9806": {"comment":"Error code $4A"},
        "9808": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "9823": {"synopsis":"The source's name to $DA31, up to and including its $FF.","comment":"The source's name"},
        "9826": {"comment":"copied to $DA31"},
        "9829": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "9830": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9833": {"comment":"Up to its $FF"},
        "9836": {"comment":"The catalogue slot"},
        "9839": {"comment":"cleared"},
        "9840": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "9842": {"synopsis":"One byte of the 13 cleared.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9846": {"synopsis":"The next matching file (see COPY_WILD).","comment":"The last name found"},
        "9849": {"comment":"is the next search's start"},
        "9852": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "9857": {"comment":"The source's name, wildcards and all"},
        "9860": {"comment":"B = 2 slots, C = 2 (LFN flags)"},
        "9863": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "9866": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG"},
        "9869": {"comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9872": {"comment":"B = the names found: none?"},
        "9873": {"comment":"IX = the directory handle"},
        "9876": {"comment":"None: COPY_WILD_END"},
        "9878": {"comment":"The name to look up"},
        "9881": {"comment":"The entry found"},
        "9884": {"comment":"BC = the source's file name: the long one goes there"},
        "9888": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_GET_LFN"},
        "9891": {"synopsis":"IDE_GET_LFN's result: a failure (or error $17 from COPY_WILD_END) goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9894": {"comment":"The destination's drive"},
        "9897": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_REF_XDPB: does it have one?"},
        "9900": {"comment":"DE = the destination's file name"},
        "9904": {"comment":"Yes: an 8.3 name"},
        "9906": {"comment":"No: the long name"},
        "9909": {"synopsis":"One byte of the long name, up to and including its $FF.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9910": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "9912": {"comment":"Up to its $FF"},
        "9915": {"comment":"On"},
        "9917": {"synopsis":"An XDPB drive: the 8 name characters up to a space, '.', the 3 type characters up to a space\n(COPY_TO_SPACE, bit 7 off); a '.' with nothing after it removed.","comment":"The name's 8 characters"},
        "9920": {"comment":"up to a space"},
        "9925": {"comment":"Then '.'"},
        "9932": {"comment":"and the type's 3 characters"},
        "9937": {"comment":"The last character"},
        "9938": {"comment":"A '.' (no type)?"},
        "9941": {"comment":"Yes: overwritten"},
        "9943": {"comment":"No: kept"},
        "9944": {"synopsis":"The $FF after the name.","comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "9947": {"synopsis":"The names ready: BREAK tested in bank 0 (ROM 1's BREAK_STOP) unless $D7FD bit 7 is set.","comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9951": {"comment":"Yes: no BREAK test"},
        "9953": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9956": {"comment":"ROM 1's BREAK_STOP, back at $26F3"},
        "9971": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9974": {"synopsis":"The file copied (COPY_ONE); the next match.","comment":"The file copied"},
        "9977": {"comment":"The next match"},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"No more matches: none copied is error $17 (through COPY_GOT_LFN's JP NC).","comment":"Files copied"},
        "9983": {"comment":"None?"},
        "9984": {"comment":"Error $17"},
        "9986": {"comment":"Through COPY_GOT_LFN's JP NC"},
        "9988": {"synopsis":"Every file copied: unless $D7FD bit 7 is set, the count from $D7FE (NUM_OUT_5, blanks before\nit) and \" files copied\" with ENTER (MSG_N_COPIED); SCR_CT = $17; then CAT_SORT_FREE.","comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "9992": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "9993": {"comment":"HL = the count of files"},
        "9998": {"comment":"Blanks before it"},
        "10000": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10003": {"comment":"ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, back at $2722"},
        "10018": {"comment":"\" files copied\", two ENTERs"},
        "10024": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $17"},
        "10029": {"synopsis":"Releases the memory a sorted DOS_CATALOG took: ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG ($011E) with B = 2, C =\n$20 and A = 0 (an unsorted call, as the API document advises), DE = $F700, HL = $E090.\nExit: what DOS_CATALOG returns.","comment":"B = 2 slots, C = $20 (A's filter)"},
        "10032": {"comment":"A = 0: no sorting"},
        "10033": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "10036": {"comment":"The name"},
        "10039": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG"},
        "10043": {"synopsis":"Copies one file, the source named at $E090 and the destination at $D827 (bank 7, $FF-ended):\nSCR_CT = $FF. Unless $D7FD bit 7 is set the source's name and \" --> \" are printed, and the\ndestination's name and ENTER after it.\n1. The source opened as file 0 for reading (ROM 2's DOS_OPEN: BC = $0001, DE = $0002), the\n   destination as file 1 for writing (BC = $0102, DE = $0204); COPY_DATA copies the bytes;\n   file 1 closed; $D7FE + 1.\n2. When the source has a metadata file (ROM 2's META_NAME builds its name at $F700), it is\n   copied too: opened as file 0, the destination's metadata name built, its directories made\n   (ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS), opened as file 1, COPY_DATA, file 1 closed.\nA failure goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"$FF"},
        "10045": {"comment":"SCR_CT: no 'scroll?'"},
        "10048": {"comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "10052": {"comment":"Yes: no names shown"},
        "10054": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "10057": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG, back at $2758"},
        "10072": {"comment":"\" --> \""},
        "10078": {"synopsis":"The source opened as file 0.","comment":"The source"},
        "10081": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "10084": {"comment":"Open action 2 (no header), create action 0"},
        "10087": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "10090": {"synopsis":"A failed open or close goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10093": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "10096": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10097": {"comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "10101": {"comment":"Yes: not shown"},
        "10103": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG, back at $2786"},
        "10118": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "10121": {"synopsis":"The destination opened as file 1, then the copy.","comment":"The destination"},
        "10122": {"comment":"File 1, exclusive-write"},
        "10125": {"comment":"Open action 4 (erase it), create action 2"},
        "10128": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "10131": {"comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10133": {"comment":"The bytes copied"},
        "10136": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "10138": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "10141": {"synopsis":"File 1 closed? Then the metadata file.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10143": {"comment":"One more file copied"},
        "10147": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "10150": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME: its metadata file's name"},
        "10153": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "10155": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "10158": {"comment":"Open action 2, create action 0"},
        "10161": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "10164": {"comment":"Not there: done"},
        "10166": {"comment":"The destination's name"},
        "10169": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME"},
        "10172": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "10174": {"comment":"None: file 0 closed"},
        "10176": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS: its directories"},
        "10179": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "10181": {"comment":"Failed: file 0 closed"},
        "10183": {"comment":"File 1, exclusive-write"},
        "10186": {"comment":"Open action 4, create action 2"},
        "10189": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "10192": {"comment":"Opened: the bytes copied"},
        "10195": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "10197": {"synopsis":"File B closed.","comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "10200": {"synopsis":"ENTER unless $D7FD bit 7 is set.","comment":"$D7FD bit 7: quiet?"},
        "10204": {"comment":"Yes: no ENTER"},
        "10205": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER through ROM 3's PRINT_A in bank 0, then pages bank 7 back in.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "10207": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10210": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "10213": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10217": {"synopsis":"Copies file 0 into file 1 in 2K pieces through $F700 (bank 7), showing the K copied so far:\na space, then for each piece the count (PRINT_K_SIZE, six characters), read by ROM 2's\nDOS_READ ($0112: B = 0, C = 7, DE = $0800) and written by DOS_WRITE ($0115: B = 1, C = 7);\nthe count is backspaced over before the next. The file's end (error $19) closes file 0 and\nwrites what was read; a piece shorter than 2K ends the copy.\nExit: carry when done; NC with A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A space before the count"},
        "10219": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10222": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "10225": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10228": {"comment":"The count of K, 0"},
        "10233": {"synopsis":"One piece: the count (HL high word, DE low word, in K) printed.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "10235": {"comment":"BCDE = the count"},
        "10237": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10240": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10243": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10246": {"comment":"File 0, into bank 7"},
        "10249": {"comment":"2K"},
        "10252": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10253": {"comment":"At $F700"},
        "10256": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_READ"},
        "10259": {"comment":"All read"},
        "10261": {"comment":"Error $19, the file's end?"},
        "10263": {"comment":"No: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10266": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "10267": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "10269": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "10272": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "10273": {"comment":"HL = 2K"},
        "10274": {"synopsis":"An error leaves through COPY_CLOSE_TEST (DOS_FAIL); otherwise DE = the bytes read.","comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10277": {"comment":"HL = the bytes read"},
        "10280": {"comment":"into DE"},
        "10283": {"synopsis":"All 2K read.","comment":"DE = 2K"},
        "10284": {"synopsis":"DE bytes written (none when DE is 0).","comment":"Nothing to write?"},
        "10288": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "10289": {"comment":"From $F700"},
        "10292": {"comment":"File 1, from bank 7"},
        "10295": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_WRITE"},
        "10298": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "10299": {"comment":"An error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "10301": {"comment":"Exactly 2K?"},
        "10305": {"comment":"(the high byte 8)"},
        "10308": {"comment":"No: the last piece"},
        "10310": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "10312": {"comment":"Backspaced over"},
        "10315": {"comment":"2K more"},
        "10320": {"comment":"HL = HL x 2 + the carry, the high word"},
        "10324": {"comment":"The next piece"},
        "10326": {"synopsis":"The last piece: the count backspaced over, the result kept in AF.","comment":"The count"},
        "10328": {"comment":"The result kept"},
        "10329": {"comment":"Backspaced over"},
        "10332": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10334": {"synopsis":"Prints six backspaces (code 8) through ROM 3's PRINT_A in bank 0, back to bank 7 after each.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"Six backspaces"},
        "10336": {"synopsis":"One backspace.","comment":"Code 8"},
        "10338": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10341": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "10344": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10347": {"comment":"The next"},
        "10350": {"synopsis":"\" files copied\" and two ENTERs, bit 7 on the last (COPY_FILES_DONE)."},
        "10365": {"synopsis":"\" --> \", bit 7 on the last space (COPY_ONE, between the names)."},
        "10370": {"synopsis":"ERASE \"name\": deletes the files the name matches (reached from NextZXOS ROM 1's\nALT_ROM_2882). The name (NAME_ARG: empty is error code $2C) copied to $E090 in bank 7 and\nparsed (PARSE_FILESPEC); no file name in it is error code $2C. With a wildcard the question\n\"Erase \" (ROM 1's $2A7C, PRINT_LOWER_TEXT), the name and \"? (Y/N)\" (ASK_YES_NO from $2B6F)\ncomes first: an NZ answer returns. Then ROM 2's DOS_DELETE ($0124) and DOS_RESULT.","comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "10373": {"comment":"To $E090 in bank 7"},
        "10376": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10377": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10378": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2899"},
        "10393": {"comment":"HL = $E090"},
        "10395": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10398": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "10401": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "10404": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10407": {"comment":"Bit 3 clear: no file name, an error"},
        "10412": {"synopsis":"A name: does it have a wildcard (C bit 2)?","comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard?"},
        "10414": {"comment":"No: delete at once"},
        "10416": {"comment":"\"Erase \" (NextZXOS ROM 1's MSG_ERASE)"},
        "10419": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_LOWER_TEXT, back at $28C2"},
        "10434": {"comment":"The name"},
        "10436": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10439": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG, back at $28D6"},
        "10454": {"synopsis":"The name printed: \"? (Y/N)\" and the key (ROM 1's $2B6F, in ASK_YES_NO).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10457": {"comment":"\"? (Y/N)\" and the key: ROM 1's $2B6F"},
        "10472": {"synopsis":"NZ (no) returns; otherwise the files are deleted in bank 7.","comment":"The name back"},
        "10473": {"comment":"NZ: not deleted"},
        "10474": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10477": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_DELETE"},
        "10480": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10482": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"a\" TO \"b\" (the syntax table's word at $04E1, after classes $0A and $0C): the second\nname (NAME_ARG) starting '+' or '-' is MOVE_ATTRIB; otherwise it goes to $E090 and the first\nto $D827 (bank 7, $FF-ended) and ROM 2's DOS_RENAME ($0127) renames the file (HL = the old\nname, DE = the new); then DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The second name (on top of the stack)"},
        "10485": {"comment":"Its first character"},
        "10486": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "10488": {"comment":"An attribute change"},
        "10491": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "10496": {"comment":"The new name to $E090"},
        "10499": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10500": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10501": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2914"},
        "10516": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10519": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "10522": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10525": {"comment":"The old name"},
        "10528": {"comment":"to $D827"},
        "10531": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10532": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10533": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2934"},
        "10548": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10551": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "10554": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10557": {"comment":"HL = the old name"},
        "10558": {"comment":"DE = the new name"},
        "10559": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10562": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_RENAME"},
        "10565": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10567": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"d:\" IN \"partition\" (the syntax table's word at $04DA): maps drive d to a partition, a\ndevice or an image file:\n1. The second string (PART_NAME_ARG): \"u>name\" is partition name of unit u, looked for by\n   ROM 2's IDE_PARTITION_FIND ($00B5, HL = $F752) for BC, its number; \"u>\" alone the unit\n   itself; anything else an image file ($D827, A = $FF).\n2. The drive (DRIVE_ARG, L = its letter); ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP ($00F1: A = the unit, BC = the\n   partition or the image's name).\nThen DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The partition, device or image"},
        "10570": {"comment":"A = the unit (or $FF, an image)"},
        "10571": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10572": {"comment":"No partition name: BC as it is"},
        "10574": {"comment":"The partition's name"},
        "10577": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10580": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PARTITION_FIND: BC = its number"},
        "10583": {"comment":"Not found: the error"},
        "10585": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10588": {"synopsis":"The drive letter (DRIVE_ARG) and ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP.","comment":"The partition (or the image's name) kept"},
        "10589": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "10592": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "10593": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "10594": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10597": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_MAP"},
        "10600": {"synopsis":"Ends a ROM 2 call: bank 0; carry returns; otherwise ROM 1's DOS_ERROR reports the error in\nA.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10603": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10604": {"comment":"ROM 1's DOS_ERROR, which reports A"},
        "10619": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"d:\" OUT (the syntax table's word at $04DD): the drive letter (DRIVE_ARG) and ROM 2's\nIDE_DOS_UNMAP ($00F4); then DOS_RESULT.","comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "10622": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10625": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_DOS_UNMAP"},
        "10628": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10630": {"synopsis":"MOVE \"name\" TO \"+x\" or \"-x\": the second string must be two characters (error code $47\notherwise), x one of P, S or A in either case (error code $47). The attribute's bit (P 2, S\n1, A 0) goes in D to set ('+') or E to clear ('-'), and ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES ($0148)\nchanges it on the file (the first string, at $F700); then DOS_RESULT.\nThe same job as the +3E's MOVE_ATTRIB.","comment":"The length"},
        "10631": {"comment":"less 2"},
        "10633": {"comment":"0: two characters?"},
        "10634": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10636": {"comment":"Error code $47"},
        "10638": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "10653": {"synopsis":"B = the sign; the letter, as a capital, must be P, S or A.","comment":"B = the sign"},
        "10655": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "10657": {"comment":"As a capital"},
        "10659": {"comment":"P?"},
        "10663": {"comment":"S?"},
        "10667": {"comment":"A?"},
        "10671": {"comment":"None of them: error code $47"},
        "10673": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "10688": {"synopsis":"The sign and the letter kept; the file's name (NAME_ARG, not empty) to $F700 in bank 7, $FF\nafter it.","comment":"The sign kept"},
        "10689": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "10690": {"comment":"The file's name (not empty)"},
        "10693": {"comment":"to $F700"},
        "10696": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10697": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $29D8"},
        "10712": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10715": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "10718": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10721": {"comment":"No bits to set or clear"},
        "10724": {"comment":"C will hold the bit"},
        "10726": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "10727": {"comment":"P?"},
        "10729": {"comment":"No"},
        "10731": {"comment":"P: bit 2"},
        "10735": {"synopsis":"S: bit 1.","comment":"S?"},
        "10737": {"comment":"No: A"},
        "10739": {"comment":"S: bit 1"},
        "10743": {"synopsis":"A: bit 0.","comment":"A: bit 0"},
        "10745": {"synopsis":"A = the sign: '+' puts the bit in D (to set), '-' in E (to clear).","comment":"The sign (B, pushed with C)"},
        "10746": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "10748": {"comment":"No: clear"},
        "10750": {"comment":"'+': D, the bits to set"},
        "10753": {"synopsis":"'-': the bit in E.","comment":"'-': E, the bits to clear"},
        "10754": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES on the name at $F700 (bank 7).","comment":"The name"},
        "10757": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10760": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES"},
        "10763": {"comment":"The result"},
        "10766": {"synopsis":"Takes a partition, device or image name from the calculator stack (ROM 1's STK_FETCH); a\nstring of 0 or 1 characters, or of 256 or more, is error code $2C:\n1. One or two digits and '>' first: the digits are the unit (D). Nothing after the '>'\n   returns NC with D = the unit. Otherwise the rest (16 characters at most, error code $2C)\n   goes to $F752 in bank 7, padded to 16 with spaces from NextZXOS ROM 1's $3FA8, and\n   returns with carry.\n2. Otherwise the whole string is an image file's name: IMAGE_NAME_ARG.\nExit: carry and D = the unit, the name at $F752; NC and D = the unit (no name); NC, D = $FF\nand BC = $D827, an image file's name ($FF-ended).\nThe same job as the +3E's PART_NAME_ARG.","comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH, back at $2A1D"},
        "10781": {"comment":"256 characters or more?"},
        "10783": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "10785": {"comment":"Fewer than 2?"},
        "10788": {"comment":"No: go on"},
        "10790": {"synopsis":"Error code $2C (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "10792": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "10807": {"synopsis":"The digits read (DIGIT_ACC); a '>' must follow them.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "10808": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "10809": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10810": {"comment":"The unit, 0 so far"},
        "10812": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "10815": {"comment":"No: an image file's name"},
        "10817": {"comment":"A second digit, if any"},
        "10820": {"comment":"D = the unit"},
        "10821": {"comment":"Nothing left?"},
        "10823": {"comment":"Then not a partition"},
        "10825": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "10828": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "10830": {"comment":"No: an image file's name"},
        "10832": {"comment":"Drop the start"},
        "10833": {"comment":"Drop the length"},
        "10834": {"comment":"The name's length"},
        "10836": {"comment":"None: the unit alone (NC)"},
        "10837": {"comment":"More than 16?"},
        "10839": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "10841": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "10842": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "10843": {"comment":"The name to $F752"},
        "10846": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2A6D"},
        "10861": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "10862": {"comment":"16 - the length"},
        "10865": {"comment":"None: no padding"},
        "10867": {"comment":"Spaces in NextZXOS ROM 1"},
        "10870": {"comment":"BC = the spaces wanted"},
        "10871": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2A86"},
        "10886": {"synopsis":"Carry: a partition name; D = the unit.","comment":"Carry: a partition's name"},
        "10887": {"comment":"D = the unit"},
        "10889": {"synopsis":"An image file: the string to $D827 in bank 7 and an $FF after it (the byte at NextZXOS ROM\n1's $0004); BC = $D827, D = $FF, NC.","comment":"HL = the string"},
        "10890": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "10891": {"comment":"The image's name to $D827"},
        "10894": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10895": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2A9E"},
        "10910": {"comment":"NextZXOS ROM 1's $0004, an $FF"},
        "10913": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "10916": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2AB3"},
        "10931": {"comment":"BC = $D827, the image's name"},
        "10932": {"comment":"D = $FF: an image file"},
        "10934": {"comment":"NC: no partition name"},
        "10936": {"synopsis":"Adds the decimal digit at HL to E (E = E x 10 + the digit), HL and BC moved on past it.\nExit: NC when it was a digit; carry, nothing changed, when not.\nChanges: AF, D, E, HL, BC.","comment":"The character as a digit"},
        "10939": {"comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "10940": {"comment":"D = 10"},
        "10942": {"comment":"10 or more?"},
        "10943": {"comment":"Carry then, NC for a digit"},
        "10944": {"comment":"Not a digit"},
        "10945": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10947": {"comment":"DE = E x 10"},
        "10949": {"comment":"plus the digit"},
        "10951": {"comment":"NC: a digit"},
        "10953": {"synopsis":"An $FF put at DE (after a name copied to $F700), then ROM 2's IDE_PATH ($01B1) with A = the\nreason code and HL = $F700.\nExit: HL = $F700; carry when done, NC with A = the error.","comment":"HL = the end of the name"},
        "10954": {"comment":"$FF there"},
        "10956": {"comment":"The name"},
        "10959": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10960": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH, reason A"},
        "10963": {"comment":"HL = $F700"},
        "10965": {"synopsis":"CD \"path\" (token $A0; the syntax table's word at $03B4, after classes $0A and $0C): the path\n(NAME_TO_F700) $FF-ended in bank 7, then ROM 2's CD_NAME ($0506), which changes the drive\nand directory; done, ROM 2's $1BE0 with A = $FF makes the default drive the LOAD and SAVE\ndrive ($5B79, $5B7A). Then PATH_RESULT.","comment":"The path to $F700"},
        "10968": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10971": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "10974": {"comment":"ROM 2's CD_NAME"},
        "10977": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10979": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "10981": {"comment":"ROM 2's $1BE0: LOAD and SAVE drives = the default"},
        "10984": {"synopsis":"DOS_RESULT.","comment":"The result"},
        "10987": {"synopsis":"MKDIR \"path\" (token $A1; the syntax table's word at $03B8): IDE_PATH with A = 2\n(rc_path_make) on the name; then PATH_RESULT.","comment":"The name to $F700"},
        "10990": {"comment":"2: rc_path_make"},
        "10992": {"synopsis":"IDE_PATH (PATH_CALL) with reason A, in bank 7.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10995": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH"},
        "10998": {"comment":"The result"},
        "11000": {"synopsis":"RMDIR \"path\" (token $A2; the syntax table's word at $03BC): IDE_PATH with A = 3\n(rc_path_delete).","comment":"The name to $F700"},
        "11003": {"comment":"3: rc_path_delete"},
        "11007": {"synopsis":"PWD (token $9F; the syntax table's word at $038F, class $0E): ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2 (stream\n2, an optional #n); checking ends at the statement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7:\nIDE_PATH with A = 1 (rc_path_get) and an empty location ($FF at $F700), so the current path\nis written at $F700; it is printed (ROM 1's PRINT_MSG) with ENTER after it; then PATH_RESULT\nwith carry.","comment":"ROM 1's STREAM_OPT_2, back at $2B0E"},
        "11022": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "11023": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11026": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11029": {"comment":"1: rc_path_get"},
        "11031": {"comment":"An empty location: the default drive"},
        "11034": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PATH"},
        "11037": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "11039": {"comment":"The path, $FF-ended"},
        "11043": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_MSG, back at $2B2E"},
        "11054": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "11057": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "11060": {"synopsis":"FORMAT (the syntax table's word at $03AC, class $0E), A = the character after it: FORMAT\nLINE n (FORMAT_LINE) and FORMAT LPRINT \"x\" [;\"y\"] (FORMAT_LPRINT) only check their operands\nand do nothing more when running. Otherwise a string (ROM 1's CLASS_A) and the statement's\nend; running, that is error code $52.","comment":"LINE?"},
        "11062": {"comment":"Yes: FORMAT LINE"},
        "11064": {"comment":"LPRINT?"},
        "11066": {"comment":"Yes: FORMAT LPRINT"},
        "11068": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A, back at $2B4B"},
        "11083": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11086": {"comment":"Error code $52"},
        "11088": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11103": {"synopsis":"FORMAT LINE: past LINE, a number (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6), the statement's end; then return.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_6, back at $2B6E"},
        "11118": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11121": {"comment":"Running: nothing done"},
        "11122": {"synopsis":"FORMAT LPRINT: past LPRINT, a string (ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_A), and when ';' follows another\none.","comment":"ROM 1's NEXT_CLASS_A, back at $2B81"},
        "11137": {"comment":"The character after the string"},
        "11138": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "11140": {"comment":"No"},
        "11142": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11143": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLASS_A, back at $2B96"},
        "11158": {"synopsis":"The statement's end ($0149); then return.","comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "11161": {"comment":"Running: nothing done"},
        "11162": {"synopsis":"Takes a string from the calculator stack (ROM 1's STK_FETCH): DE = its start, BC = its\nlength; an empty one is error code $2C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE (what STK_FETCH changes).","comment":"ROM 1's STK_FETCH, back at $2BA9"},
        "11177": {"comment":"The length"},
        "11179": {"comment":"Not 0: done"},
        "11180": {"synopsis":"Error code $2C (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A).","comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "11182": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11197": {"synopsis":"Copies a string from the calculator stack (NAME_ARG) to $F700 in bank 7 (ROM 1's\nCOPY_BANK0_TO_7).\nExit: HL = $F700, DE past the copy (where the caller puts its $FF).","comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "11200": {"comment":"The copy's start"},
        "11203": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11204": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11205": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2BD4"},
        "11220": {"comment":"HL = $F700"},
        "11222": {"synopsis":"Copies up to B characters from HL to DE, bit 7 off, stopping at a space (catalogue names are\npadded with spaces).\nExit: HL and DE past what was copied.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.\nThe same job as the +3E's COPY_TO_SPACE.","comment":"A space ends the name"},
        "11225": {"comment":"Done at it"},
        "11226": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "11228": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "11231": {"comment":"Up to B characters"},
        "11234": {"synopsis":"Takes a drive name from the calculator stack: copied to $E090 (NAME_TO_E090) and parsed\n(PARSE_FILESPEC). It must be a drive letter alone, such as \"C:\" (flags exactly 1), else\nerror code $4E.\nExit: L = the drive letter, bank 0.","comment":"The name to $E090"},
        "11237": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11240": {"comment":"Parsed"},
        "11243": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11246": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Flags 1: a drive letter alone?"},
        "11248": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11249": {"comment":"No: error code $4E"},
        "11251": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11266": {"synopsis":"Takes a name from the calculator stack to $E090 in bank 7 (NAME_TO_HL).","comment":"To $E090"},
        "11269": {"synopsis":"Copies a string from the calculator stack (NAME_ARG, not empty) to HL in bank 7, 255\ncharacters at most, and puts $FF after it.\nExit: HL = the copy, bank 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Kept"},
        "11270": {"comment":"DE, BC = the name (not empty)"},
        "11273": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11274": {"synopsis":"256 characters or more are cut to 255.","comment":"256 characters or more?"},
        "11276": {"comment":"No"},
        "11278": {"comment":"Yes: 255"},
        "11281": {"synopsis":"The copy (ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7).","comment":"DE = the place, HL = the string"},
        "11282": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "11283": {"comment":"ROM 1's COPY_BANK0_TO_7, back at $2C22"},
        "11298": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "11299": {"synopsis":"$FF at DE, in bank 7; bank 0.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "11302": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "11305": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11309": {"synopsis":"CAT's name to $E090 in bank 7: BC = its length and DE its start (from STK_FETCH, before\n$1FFC); an empty name becomes a lone $FF.","comment":"The place"},
        "11312": {"comment":"The length"},
        "11314": {"comment":"Not 0: copied"},
        "11316": {"comment":"DE = $E090"},
        "11317": {"comment":"Just the $FF"},
        "11319": {"synopsis":"Parses the file name at HL (bank 7, $FF-ended): an optional prefix, a user area (one or two\ndigits, below 16) and/or a drive letter (A-P, either case), ended by ':'; then a path with\n'/' or '\\' separators and the file name after the last one.\nExit: HL = the file name (past the prefix and the path); D = the drive letter and E = the\nuser area (the defaults, from ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE and DOS_SET_USER with A = $FF, unless\ngiven); A = C = flags: bit 0 a drive given, bit 1 a user area given, bit 2 a wildcard ('*'\nor '?') in the file name, bit 3 a file name follows, bit 4 a path given. A wildcard before a\nseparator is error code $2C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The name kept"},
        "11320": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "11322": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE: A = the default drive"},
        "11325": {"comment":"D = the drive"},
        "11327": {"comment":"$FF: ask"},
        "11329": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_USER: A = the default user area"},
        "11333": {"comment":"E = the user area"},
        "11334": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "11335": {"comment":"No flags yet"},
        "11337": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "11338": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "11339": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11349": {"comment":"E = the user area"},
        "11350": {"comment":"Bit 1: a user area"},
        "11352": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11354": {"comment":"A second digit?"},
        "11362": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11364": {"comment":"D = it (for now)"},
        "11365": {"comment":"E x 10"},
        "11370": {"comment":"plus the digit"},
        "11373": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "11375": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix after all"},
        "11377": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11379": {"synopsis":"After the digits: ':' ends a user-area prefix.","comment":"':'?"},
        "11381": {"comment":"Yes: a user-area prefix"},
        "11383": {"synopsis":"A drive letter A-P must be followed by ':'.","comment":"As a capital"},
        "11385": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "11387": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix"},
        "11389": {"comment":"Above 'P'?"},
        "11391": {"comment":"Yes: no prefix"},
        "11393": {"comment":"D = the drive letter"},
        "11394": {"comment":"Bit 0: a drive"},
        "11396": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11398": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "11400": {"comment":"No: no prefix"},
        "11402": {"synopsis":"A prefix: the name starts past its ':'.","comment":"Past the ':'"},
        "11403": {"comment":"Drop the old start"},
        "11404": {"comment":"The name starts here"},
        "11405": {"comment":"Then the scan"},
        "11407": {"synopsis":"No prefix (C = 0): the name starts at its first character.","comment":"No flags"},
        "11409": {"comment":"HL = the start again"},
        "11411": {"synopsis":"The name's characters, up to its $FF.","comment":"The next character"},
        "11413": {"comment":"$FF, the end?"},
        "11415": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "11417": {"comment":"Bit 3: a file name follows"},
        "11419": {"comment":"'/'?"},
        "11423": {"comment":"'\\'?"},
        "11427": {"comment":"'*'?"},
        "11431": {"comment":"'?'?"},
        "11433": {"comment":"No: the next"},
        "11435": {"synopsis":"A wildcard: bit 2.","comment":"Bit 2: a wildcard"},
        "11439": {"synopsis":"A separator: a wildcard before it is an error; otherwise bit 4 set, bit 3 cleared, and the\nfile name starts after it.","comment":"A wildcard before it?"},
        "11441": {"comment":"Yes: an error"},
        "11443": {"comment":"No file name yet"},
        "11445": {"comment":"Bit 4: a path"},
        "11447": {"comment":"Drop the old start"},
        "11448": {"comment":"The file name starts after it"},
        "11451": {"synopsis":"HL = where the file name starts; A = the flags.","comment":"HL = where the file name starts"},
        "11452": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "11454": {"synopsis":"A wildcard in the path: error code $2C, in bank 0.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "11457": {"comment":"Error code $2C"},
        "11459": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11474": {"synopsis":"Checks a rectangle on the current screen and works out the address of its top-left pixel\n(called from $106C and $147D):\n1. E (the left x) + C (the width less one) must stay within 255, and below 128 unless $5C7F\n   bit 1 is set (Layer 2, 256 x 192; otherwise LoRes, 128 x 96).\n2. B (the height) 0 is error code $0A ($121F); D (the top y) + B - 1 must stay below 192, or\n   96 for LoRes. A rectangle off the screen is error code 4, SP swapped back first ($00EC).\n3. Layer 2: PRECT_ADDRESS. LoRes: LORES_ADDRESS.\nExit: DE = the address; C = the row length less one ($FF or $7F); B = the high byte at which\nthe paged-in block ends ($40, $58 or $78).","comment":"C + E, the right edge"},
        "11476": {"comment":"Past 255: off the screen"},
        "11478": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 1: Layer 2?"},
        "11482": {"comment":"Yes: 256 wide"},
        "11484": {"comment":"LoRes: 128 wide"},
        "11488": {"synopsis":"The rows.","comment":"The height"},
        "11490": {"comment":"0: report B"},
        "11493": {"comment":"The bottom edge"},
        "11495": {"comment":"Past 255: off the screen"},
        "11497": {"comment":"Row 192 or more?"},
        "11499": {"comment":"Yes: off the screen"},
        "11501": {"comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "11505": {"comment":"Yes: on to the address"},
        "11507": {"comment":"LoRes: row 96 or more?"},
        "11509": {"comment":"No: on to the address"},
        "11511": {"synopsis":"Error code 4 (ROM 1's ERROR_128_A), SP swapped back first.","comment":"SP swapped back first"},
        "11514": {"comment":"Error code 4"},
        "11516": {"comment":"ROM 1's ERROR_128_A"},
        "11531": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: the 16K third holding row D is paged in at $0000-$3FFF for writing (port $123B,\nL2_PAGE_SET): DE = (D AND $3F) x 256 + E; BC = $40FF.","comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "11535": {"comment":"No: LORES_ADDRESS"},
        "11537": {"comment":"The row's top two bits"},
        "11540": {"comment":"B = the third (as port bits 7-6)"},
        "11541": {"comment":"D = the row within the third"},
        "11545": {"comment":"$5B7B's other bits"},
        "11550": {"comment":"The third added"},
        "11551": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 3: write paging, the shadow banks"},
        "11553": {"synopsis":"Port $123B = A, the third (bits 7-6; third 3 becomes third 0) and the paging bits, kept at\n$5B7B.","comment":"Third 3 or more?"},
        "11555": {"comment":"No"},
        "11557": {"comment":"Yes: back to the first third"},
        "11559": {"synopsis":"Port $123B written; BC = $40FF.","comment":"Kept"},
        "11562": {"comment":"Port $123B, Layer 2 access"},
        "11567": {"comment":"B = $40, the third's end; C = $FF"},
        "11571": {"synopsis":"LoRes: DE = $4000 + D x 128 + E, rows 48 and more at $6000 on; B = $58 (or $78 for the lower\nhalf); C = $7F; MMU slot 3 gets page $0B (LORES_PAGE_IN).","comment":"D / 2, the odd row bit into the carry"},
        "11573": {"comment":"An even row"},
        "11575": {"comment":"Odd: the right half of 256 bytes"},
        "11577": {"synopsis":"D = $40 + D / 2.","comment":"D + $40: at $4000 on"},
        "11579": {"comment":"B = $58, the upper half's end; C = $7F"},
        "11582": {"comment":"The address's high byte"},
        "11583": {"comment":"Below $5800?"},
        "11584": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11586": {"comment":"Rows 48 on: $6000 on"},
        "11589": {"comment":"B = $78, the lower half's end"},
        "11591": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 3 ($6000-$7FFF) = page $0B.","comment":"Page $0B"},
        "11593": {"synopsis":"NextReg $53 (MMU slot 3) = A.","comment":"MMU slot 3"},
        "11597": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 3 = page $11 again.","comment":"Page $11"},
        "11601": {"synopsis":"The next row: DE = HL (this row's start) + C + 1. When that crosses B: Layer 2 pages the\nnext third in (L2_NEXT_THIRD), LoRes moves on to the lower half at $6000 (LORES_LOWER).\nCalled from $148B.\nChanges: AF, DE, and B and the paging when a block is crossed.","comment":"DE = C + 1, the row's length"},
        "11605": {"comment":"plus the row's start"},
        "11606": {"comment":"DE = the next row's"},
        "11607": {"comment":"Still below the block's end?"},
        "11609": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "11610": {"comment":"C = $FF: Layer 2?"},
        "11612": {"comment":"No: LoRes"},
        "11614": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: D back to $00-$3F, the next third ($5B7B + $40) paged in. Also called from $113C.","comment":"D back to the third's start"},
        "11616": {"comment":"The paged third"},
        "11619": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "11621": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "11623": {"synopsis":"LoRes: on to $6000 on (D + 8); B = $78. Also called from $1148.","comment":"D + 8: on to $6000"},
        "11627": {"comment":"B = $78, the lower half's end"},
        "11630": {"synopsis":"Ends drawing (from $1159 and $1492): LoRes (C = $7F) gives MMU slot 3 page $11 back\n(LORES_PAGE_OUT); Layer 2 (C = $FF) leaves only the visibility bit of $5B7B (bit 1) in port\n$123B, so the paging is off.","comment":"C = $FF: Layer 2?"},
        "11631": {"comment":"No: page $11 back"},
        "11633": {"comment":"The visibility bit alone"},
        "11636": {"comment":"(bit 1)"},
        "11638": {"comment":"Port $123B: paging off"},
        "11640": {"synopsis":"A = the low four bits of $5C7F (the screen mode): 0 returns Z, 1-2 return with carry; 3 and\nup return A / 4 - 1 (NC). Called from $11BD and $1319.\nThe same job as NextZXOS ROM 1's MODE_5C7F_GET (the bytes are the same).","comment":"The screen mode"},
        "11643": {"comment":"Its low four bits"},
        "11645": {"comment":"0: Z"},
        "11646": {"comment":"1 or 2?"},
        "11648": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "11649": {"comment":"A / 4"},
        "11653": {"comment":"less 1"},
        "11655": {"synopsis":"Before the program is changed (NextZXOS ROM 1's AR_FINISH and MERGE_LOAD call it first):\nwhen $5B66 bit 1 is set, it is cleared and the GO SUB stack is walked from its newest entry\n(ERR_SP + 3, each entry's type byte). In each type-1 entry whose byte before the type is 0\nthe place it records (a bank byte and an offset, 8 bytes below its end) is made a line\nnumber: the line holding that place is looked for in the main program (the offset + PROG) or\nin the bank (paged in at $C000, its lines from $C002), and its number written over the\noffset (STACK_TO_PLACES turns it back). Bank $FE records no place.\nOther entries are passed: types 0 and 1 by their length word, 2-$3D by 11 bytes, $3F up by\nthe type with bit 6 cleared; $3E ends the walk.","comment":"$5B66 bit 1: places to convert?"},
        "11660": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "11661": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "11663": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "11666": {"comment":"+ 3: the newest entry's type byte"},
        "11668": {"synopsis":"HL on to the next entry's type byte."},
        "11669": {"synopsis":"An entry, by its type.","comment":"The type"},
        "11670": {"comment":"1?"},
        "11672": {"comment":"Yes: STL_TYPE_1"},
        "11674": {"comment":"0: a variable entry"},
        "11676": {"comment":"$3E, the end marker?"},
        "11678": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "11679": {"comment":"2-$3D: 11 bytes"},
        "11681": {"comment":"Higher: bit 6 off"},
        "11683": {"comment":"is the entry's size"},
        "11687": {"synopsis":"Types 0 and 1: passed by the length word after the type.","comment":"Past the type"},
        "11688": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "11692": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11695": {"synopsis":"Types 2-$3D: 11 bytes.","comment":"11 bytes on"},
        "11701": {"synopsis":"Type 1: the byte before the type not 0 is passed as STL_SKIP_VAR; 0 has a place to convert.","comment":"The byte before the type"},
        "11704": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "11705": {"comment":"Then passed as type 0"},
        "11707": {"comment":"BC = the entry's length"},
        "11712": {"comment":"HL = the entry's end"},
        "11713": {"comment":"ROM 1's RESTORE_5_BYTES, back at $2DD0"},
        "11728": {"comment":"The end kept"},
        "11729": {"comment":"8 bytes back: the place's bank"},
        "11734": {"comment":"$FE: no place"},
        "11736": {"comment":"Then nothing to do"},
        "11738": {"comment":"The offset's address"},
        "11739": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11740": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "11743": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "11746": {"comment":"$FF, the main program?"},
        "11747": {"comment":"Yes: STL_MAIN"},
        "11749": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "11750": {"comment":"Bank 7 (SP swapped)"},
        "11753": {"comment":"Its two 8K pages"},
        "11754": {"comment":"at MMU slot 6"},
        "11758": {"comment":"and 7: the bank at $C000"},
        "11761": {"comment":"The bank's first line"},
        "11764": {"comment":"The search"},
        "11766": {"synopsis":"The main program: DE = PROG + the offset.","comment":"PROG"},
        "11769": {"comment":"DE = PROG + the offset"},
        "11772": {"synopsis":"One line: BC = its number (high byte first), then past its length, until the line reaches\npast DE.","comment":"BC = the line's number"},
        "11776": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11777": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "11781": {"comment":"The text's start kept"},
        "11782": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "11783": {"comment":"Past DE?"},
        "11785": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11786": {"comment":"Yes: this line"},
        "11788": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Drop the number"},
        "11792": {"synopsis":"The line found: bank 0 again for a bank; its number written over the offset.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "11793": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "11796": {"comment":"A bank ($FF + 1 not 0)?"},
        "11797": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "11800": {"comment":"The offset's address"},
        "11801": {"comment":"The line number written over it"},
        "11804": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"The entry's end back"},
        "11805": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "11808": {"synopsis":"After the program has changed (from NextZXOS ROM 1's RUN_SETUP at $0B65 and\nLOADED_PROG_FIX): sets $5B66 bit 1 and makes the GO SUB stack's entries point at the program\nagain, keeping the current place:\n1. CH_ADD's offset from PROG_BASE (ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC), PPC and the program's bank\n   ($5B77) saved.\n2. Each 11-byte entry (types 2-$3D and $4B) is found again by its line (PPC, entry bytes\n   7-8) and statement (byte 9): NXTLIN's and CH_ADD's offsets (bytes 5-6 and 3-4) and $5EB6\n   (bytes 1-2) are set again. CH_ADD's place: for type $22 after PROC name(...) (possibly\n   after BANK n), for $4B after ON ERROR, for the others the next statement. An entry whose\n   line or statement is gone, or that belongs to a direct command (PPC bit 15), gets bank\n   $FE.\n3. Each type-1 entry with a line number (from STACK_TO_LINES): the variable is looked for in\n   the line's PRIVATE statements (token $82), each name after a hidden number; its number's\n   place is written back as the entry's offset. Not found: bank $FE and the name's low five\n   bits $1E.\n4. At the end ($3E) the bank, PPC, NXTLIN and CH_ADD are set again.","comment":"Places held from now on"},
        "11813": {"comment":"ROM 1's PROG_BASE_PPC, back at $2E34"},
        "11828": {"comment":"DE = PROG_BASE"},
        "11829": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
